1
00:00:00,442 --> 00:00:05,046
[The moonlit night of the Moonlight cast]

2
00:00:05,046 --> 00:00:06,947
Let's go.

3
00:00:07,635 --> 00:00:08,846
[The air is much cooler now]
Ah, it's so much better outside.

4
00:00:08,846 --> 00:00:11,315
- Yeah, way better.
- It's amazing.

5
00:00:12,188 --> 00:00:13,399
[They seem to be startled by something]

6
00:00:13,399 --> 00:00:14,863
- That's so cool!
- What is it?

7
00:00:14,863 --> 00:00:16,707
- It's a sky lantern!
- Oh, sky lanterns!

8
00:00:16,707 --> 00:00:17,825
Where?

9
00:00:17,825 --> 00:00:20,077
[What awaits the Moonlight cast...]
Wow!

10
00:00:20,077 --> 00:00:23,283
[are colorful sky lanterns!]
Oh, so pretty!

11
00:00:23,283 --> 00:00:25,440
Now that's a touching sight.

12
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:27,757
[The Moonlight cast have gathered underneath]
So pretty, look!

13
00:00:27,757 --> 00:00:30,964
[They'll be watching a video together]
I see, so we're watching it on a big screen.

14
00:00:32,739 --> 00:00:34,769
<i>Mighty God of the sky!</i>

15
00:00:34,769 --> 00:00:36,719
[That scene, from 10 years ago, revisited...]
<i>Mighty God of the sky!</i>

16
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:40,032
<i>Let our town prosper
and grant us a bountiful harvest!</i>

17
00:00:40,032 --> 00:00:41,583
- Oh, I remember this.
- Ah, I'm getting goosebumps!

18
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:44,219
[Happy feet]
I don't know what to do!

19
00:00:44,219 --> 00:00:47,025
[Love in the Moonlight, episode 5]

20
00:00:47,025 --> 00:00:50,265
[The scene where people are floating
sky lanterns with wishes written on them]

21
00:00:57,605 --> 00:00:59,856
This music makes my heart swell...

22
00:00:59,856 --> 00:01:01,000
every time I hear it.

23
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,377
[Makes eye contact]

24
00:01:02,377 --> 00:01:03,810
How pretty!

25
00:01:06,719 --> 00:01:08,452
Oh, there it is.

26
00:01:08,452 --> 00:01:11,359
[Yoon Seong interrupts Lee Yeong and Ra On's
sky lantern festival date]

27
00:01:11,359 --> 00:01:14,972
<i>Your Highness, I apologize,
but I've arranged a meeting with Eunuch Hong.</i>

28
00:01:15,875 --> 00:01:17,479
<i>I sincerely apologize, Your Highness.</i>

29
00:01:17,479 --> 00:01:19,989
- Oh, so cute!
- How adorable is that?

30
00:01:19,989 --> 00:01:22,035
This is embarrassing.

31
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:36,065
<i>I shall not allow it.</i>

32
00:01:38,719 --> 00:01:40,032
<i>Your Highness.</i>

33
00:01:45,199 --> 00:01:46,559
<i>She is mine.</i>

34
00:01:48,065 --> 00:01:51,772
[Love in the Moonlight's iconic line]
<i>She is mine.</i>

35
00:01:53,652 --> 00:01:55,259
Stop fighting!

36
00:01:55,259 --> 00:01:57,599
[Death glare]

37
00:01:57,599 --> 00:01:59,563
Why were you so mad?

38
00:01:59,563 --> 00:02:02,365
[Sir Yoon Seong, angry as can be]
He's so mad, look!

39
00:02:02,365 --> 00:02:06,405
[The famous scene, revisited in 10 years]

40
00:02:07,192 --> 00:02:10,003
Watching this scene again
after such a long time is making me...

41
00:02:10,003 --> 00:02:11,252
- Making you what?
- All mushy and soft?

42
00:02:11,252 --> 00:02:13,205
Yes, I feel all mushy and soft inside.

43
00:02:13,205 --> 00:02:16,490
Well, when I heard the music
from the opening of the scene...

44
00:02:16,490 --> 00:02:18,599
You Jung and I kind of locked eyes.

45
00:02:18,599 --> 00:02:20,236
[As if the music took them back to the past]
It gave me goosebumps!

46
00:02:20,236 --> 00:02:22,687
It felt like we'd slipped in time,
to a decade ago.

47
00:02:22,687 --> 00:02:24,171
What were you so mad about?

48
00:02:24,171 --> 00:02:25,865
Me?

49
00:02:25,865 --> 00:02:28,399
Well, it's humiliating, isn't it?

50
00:02:28,399 --> 00:02:30,449
[We promised to meet first...]
A promise is a promise, you know.

51
00:02:30,449 --> 00:02:31,792
- Bo Gum.
- Yeah?

52
00:02:31,792 --> 00:02:33,919
[2026 ver. I shall not allow it. She is mine]
Give us a new and updated 2026 version

53
00:02:33,919 --> 00:02:35,444
of that famous quote.

54
00:02:35,444 --> 00:02:36,533
[Excited giggle]

55
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:38,351
We'll have to go the whole way, then!

56
00:02:38,351 --> 00:02:39,632
[1 - Look at Ra On]
Look at me,

57
00:02:39,632 --> 00:02:40,789
[2 - Grab Ra On's hand]
and then grab,

58
00:02:40,789 --> 00:02:42,223
[3 - Look at Yoon Seong]
and while staring at Jin Young...

59
00:02:43,392 --> 00:02:45,792
Oh, I'll be staring.

60
00:02:45,792 --> 00:02:47,905
[Reenacting the death glare]
It's exactly the same as the show!

61
00:02:47,905 --> 00:02:49,965
If we're going for accuracy...

62
00:02:49,965 --> 00:02:52,544
I'm actually in the scene,
way back over there, flying sky lanterns.

63
00:02:52,544 --> 00:02:53,822
Oh, that's right!

64
00:02:53,822 --> 00:02:57,105
[Byeong Yeon joins the reenactment]
Yeah, that's right! That's right.

65
00:02:57,105 --> 00:03:00,356
[Byeong Yeon was flying sky lanterns all alone,
away from Lee Yeong and Ra On]

66
00:03:00,356 --> 00:03:04,872
<i>On our very last moment,
may we be good friends.</i>

67
00:03:04,872 --> 00:03:07,965
[Sulking away]

68
00:03:07,965 --> 00:03:08,989
"On our very last moment..."

69
00:03:08,989 --> 00:03:10,732
[Recreating that lonely scene]
Yeah, you looked so sad!

70
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,659
- "may we be good friends."
- This is how it should be!

71
00:03:12,659 --> 00:03:13,749
What was Ha Yeon doing then?

72
00:03:13,749 --> 00:03:16,289
Yeah, I think I was at home.

73
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:18,752
[The truth is...]
<i>I'll take a sky lantern.</i>

74
00:03:18,752 --> 00:03:20,339
[Ha Yeon had been buying a sky lantern]
<i>That's four coins, ma'am!</i>

75
00:03:20,339 --> 00:03:22,063
[Lost her money]

76
00:03:22,063 --> 00:03:23,853
[She ends up owing a lantern...]
<i>Give the lantern to anyone who has a wish,</i>

77
00:03:23,853 --> 00:03:25,993
[to Lee Yeong]
<i>but no money to give.</i>

78
00:03:27,012 --> 00:03:28,623
[Ha Yeon and Byeong Yeon are ready]
Oh, so cute.

79
00:03:28,623 --> 00:03:30,665
[Buying a lantern] [Flying solo]
So cute!

80
00:03:30,665 --> 00:03:33,072
[2026 ver.
'I shall not allow it. She is mine']

81
00:03:35,985 --> 00:03:37,620
Your Highness.

82
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:40,965
I must apologize,
but I have preordained a meeting.

83
00:03:40,965 --> 00:03:42,429
I apologize, Your Highness.

84
00:03:42,429 --> 00:03:43,507
Let's go.

85
00:03:43,507 --> 00:03:46,379
I shall not allow it.

86
00:03:46,379 --> 00:03:48,034
I shall not allow it.

87
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:51,439
[Giving him the death glare]

88
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:54,205
[Enjoying the front row view]

89
00:04:02,103 --> 00:04:03,864
She is mine.

90
00:04:05,785 --> 00:04:07,925
[Can't keep in character]

91
00:04:07,925 --> 00:04:10,183
[It's kind of embarrassing after 10 years]

92
00:04:10,183 --> 00:04:11,613
It's sort of awkward, isn't it?

93
00:04:11,613 --> 00:04:14,279
It just doesn't feel the same, you know.

94
00:04:14,279 --> 00:04:16,183
But I really liked it. It was cool.

95
00:04:16,183 --> 00:04:17,827
[Volley of praises]
You were really charismatic.

96
00:04:17,827 --> 00:04:19,713
Really? Thank you.

97
00:04:21,512 --> 00:04:23,165
- Ah, w-what is that?
- What?

98
00:04:23,165 --> 00:04:24,823
[What startled her this much?]
- Ah, w-what is that? - What?

99
00:04:24,823 --> 00:04:27,079
- What is this?
- Hello, it's nice to meet you.

100
00:04:28,259 --> 00:04:30,085
[Bo Gum gets handed a mic]
What is this?

101
00:04:30,085 --> 00:04:32,099
Hello, it's nice to meet you.

102
00:04:32,099 --> 00:04:33,376
[Hyped to see what's going on]
What's happening?

103
00:04:33,376 --> 00:04:34,967
Should I stand up?

104
00:04:34,967 --> 00:04:37,145
[The surprise event has left them speechless]
What is this?

105
00:04:37,145 --> 00:04:38,796
- Music Bank?
- Music...

106
00:04:38,796 --> 00:04:40,853
- Bank!
- No, no. Nothing like that.

107
00:04:40,853 --> 00:04:43,644
This is... Moonlight Cantabile!

108
00:04:46,025 --> 00:04:47,845
[Bo Gum, former MC, planned a special event]
I welcome you all who have joined us today

109
00:04:47,845 --> 00:04:48,865
on Moonlight Cantabile.

110
00:04:48,865 --> 00:04:50,852
I am your surprise host, Park Bo Gum.

111
00:04:50,852 --> 00:04:52,623
[Excitement to the max!]

112
00:04:52,623 --> 00:04:53,647
This is awesome!

113
00:04:53,647 --> 00:04:56,005
Everyone's having a special time here.

114
00:04:56,005 --> 00:04:58,776
- Are you having fun?
- Yes, we are!

115
00:04:58,776 --> 00:05:00,200
If you're happy, give me a...

116
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,245
[Pause]

117
00:05:01,245 --> 00:05:02,545
- A good scream?
- Why did you stop?

118
00:05:02,545 --> 00:05:03,792
Let's not yell.

119
00:05:03,792 --> 00:05:05,382
Give me a happy giggle!

120
00:05:07,012 --> 00:05:09,572
[The Moonlight cast listens well
to the class president]

121
00:05:09,572 --> 00:05:11,769
Thank you. The reason I have a mic

122
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:16,049
on this meaningful day is that...

123
00:05:16,049 --> 00:05:18,700
to celebrate the 10th anniversary, we have...

124
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:21,171
- I knew it!
- I knew this was coming!

125
00:05:21,171 --> 00:05:24,652
[What's a party without a special guest?]
a very special guest with us today.

126
00:05:24,652 --> 00:05:28,840
When thinking of the 'Moonlight' crew,
who comes to your mind first?

127
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,085
[Director Kim of 'Love in the Moonlight']
Kim Seong Yoon!

128
00:05:30,085 --> 00:05:31,592
- Director Kim, you say?
- Yes!

129
00:05:31,592 --> 00:05:34,672
When I first heard of our special guest,
I thought,

130
00:05:34,672 --> 00:05:36,916
'Wow, no way!'

131
00:05:36,916 --> 00:05:38,379
'No way this is who's coming!'

132
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:39,456
[It's that big of a surprise?]

133
00:05:39,456 --> 00:05:41,239
- I couldn't believe it.
- Is it Mr. Cheon Ho Jin?

134
00:05:41,239 --> 00:05:42,596
- Like, 'really?'
- Mr. Cheon Ho Jin?

135
00:05:42,596 --> 00:05:44,247
Oh, I want to see him!

136
00:05:44,247 --> 00:05:45,872
Mr. Cheon Ho Jin!

137
00:05:45,872 --> 00:05:48,116
[Is the mystery guest actor Cheon Ho Jin?]
We miss you, Mr. Cheon Ho Jin!

138
00:05:48,116 --> 00:05:50,700
- Now, let's welcome today's guest...
- Who is it? Where are they?

139
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,124
with a big applause!

140
00:05:52,124 --> 00:05:54,192
[Clapping anyway]

141
00:05:54,192 --> 00:05:56,059
[Stands up to properly greet the guest]

142
00:05:56,059 --> 00:05:58,519
- Who is it?
- Who are you?

143
00:05:58,519 --> 00:06:00,116
- Hello, everyone!
- What?

144
00:06:00,116 --> 00:06:02,733
- Hello!
- What? They're going to sing?

145
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:05,479
[Mic stands appear out of nowhere]
What? They're going to sing?

146
00:06:05,479 --> 00:06:07,776
- Maybe they worked on the OST.
- Oh, that could be it!

147
00:06:07,776 --> 00:06:09,527
[Is it the singer Gummy?]
No way!

148
00:06:09,527 --> 00:06:11,104
What if it's Gummy?

149
00:06:11,104 --> 00:06:12,488
[They have two mic stands]
But look, it must be a duet song.

150
00:06:12,488 --> 00:06:14,379
[Is it Soyou and Yoo Seung Woo?]
Maybe it's Soyou and Yoo Seung Woo?

151
00:06:14,379 --> 00:06:16,383
- Ms. Soyou and Mr. Yoo Seung Woo...
- I can't believe it.

152
00:06:16,383 --> 00:06:19,739
[They came all the way here to Gangwon state]
Now, come to grace 'Moonlight Cantabile',

153
00:06:19,739 --> 00:06:22,356
[So who is it?]
our guest of the day...

154
00:06:22,356 --> 00:06:24,539
Give them a big applause!

155
00:06:24,539 --> 00:06:28,112
[Starts clapping anyway]

156
00:06:28,112 --> 00:06:29,577
[Please come out, now...]
Come out!

157
00:06:29,577 --> 00:06:31,480
- Come out, please!
- Where are you?

158
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,972
I'll go get them.

159
00:06:32,972 --> 00:06:35,205
- Huh? You'll go get them?
- Where are you?

160
00:06:35,205 --> 00:06:37,892
[MC Bo Gum is off to get the guest]

161
00:06:40,705 --> 00:06:45,485
[and the rest of the Moonlight cast
starts a welcome song]

162
00:06:45,485 --> 00:06:48,132
[So... when are they coming?]

163
00:06:51,039 --> 00:06:52,385
Aw, come on!

164
00:06:53,419 --> 00:06:54,359
[Coming through]

165
00:07:02,639 --> 00:07:05,405
[A familiar face enters with a bow...]

166
00:07:05,405 --> 00:07:08,672
[and the eldest heads
for the stage with a grin]

167
00:07:08,672 --> 00:07:11,583
[Hi, we're here to celebrate!]

168
00:07:11,583 --> 00:07:12,748
Our special guest,

169
00:07:12,748 --> 00:07:14,292
[A truly touching reveal, surely!]
I knew it!

170
00:07:14,292 --> 00:07:16,812
Give a round of applause for
Park Bo Gum and Jin Young!

171
00:07:16,812 --> 00:07:19,499
They've come to make today truly special,

172
00:07:19,499 --> 00:07:20,996
[They are the special guests]
Park Bo Gum and Jin Young!

173
00:07:20,996 --> 00:07:22,165
Give them a big round of applause!

174
00:07:22,165 --> 00:07:23,904
[An aggressive welcome is due]

175
00:07:23,904 --> 00:07:26,025
Hello, we are from 'Love in the Moonlight,'

176
00:07:26,025 --> 00:07:29,923
and we're the Moonlight Princes,
Park Bo Gum and Jin Young.

177
00:07:30,972 --> 00:07:32,132
[Out of words]

178
00:07:32,132 --> 00:07:34,712
[Bo Gum and Jin Young as 'Moonlight Princes']
Today, to celebrate the 10th anniversary,

179
00:07:34,712 --> 00:07:36,876
we've decided to have a debut stage.

180
00:07:36,876 --> 00:07:39,507
- We thank you wholeheartedly for having us.
- A debut stage?

181
00:07:39,507 --> 00:07:40,531
[Super nervous]
This is hilarious!

182
00:07:40,531 --> 00:07:44,305
We prepared this performance for today.

183
00:07:44,305 --> 00:07:46,285
'Misty Road.'

184
00:07:46,285 --> 00:07:48,812
- 'Misty Road.'
- Wait, what? Really?

185
00:07:48,812 --> 00:07:50,642
I can't wait!

186
00:07:50,642 --> 00:07:52,702
['Misty Road' is one of the OSTs
from Love in the Moonlight]

187
00:07:52,702 --> 00:07:54,889
<i>Don't cry.</i>

188
00:07:54,889 --> 00:07:56,889
[Jin Young wrote it himself 10 years ago]
<i>I don't want to be that kind of guy...</i>

189
00:07:58,735 --> 00:08:01,621
<i>who makes a girl cry.</i>

190
00:08:02,593 --> 00:08:04,682
[about to be reborn by the Moonlight Princes]
Misty Road.

191
00:08:04,682 --> 00:08:06,606
- Wow, really?
- You'll hear it from us now.

192
00:08:06,606 --> 00:08:08,564
- So handsome!
- So cool!

193
00:08:08,564 --> 00:08:09,582
Thank you all.

194
00:08:09,582 --> 00:08:11,339
Sexy dynamite!

195
00:08:11,339 --> 00:08:14,233
[An encouragement to blow away the anxiety]
Sexy dynamite!

196
00:08:15,055 --> 00:08:17,149
The lyrics... are they visible?

197
00:08:17,149 --> 00:08:20,597
Aw, come on! You're here to perform,
and you still need the lyrics?

198
00:08:20,597 --> 00:08:22,407
Well, this is our first performance ever.

199
00:08:22,407 --> 00:08:23,618
This is our debut, so...

200
00:08:23,618 --> 00:08:26,782
[These guys aren't afraid to speak their mind]
We've never even rehearsed, actually.

201
00:08:26,782 --> 00:08:29,979
It was our lifelong dream
to be a part of Park Bo Gum's 'Cantabile.'

202
00:08:29,979 --> 00:08:31,457
[Right?]

203
00:08:31,457 --> 00:08:33,208
Yeah, exactly.

204
00:08:33,208 --> 00:08:36,782
[Give the Moonlight Princes lots of love!]
Thank you, everyone.

205
00:08:36,782 --> 00:08:41,749
[Misty Road by the Moonlight Princes]

206
00:08:41,749 --> 00:08:44,489
Oh, it's a remix.

207
00:08:44,489 --> 00:08:47,929
[The new 2026 version of 'Misty Road,'
remixed by Jin Young himself]

208
00:08:47,929 --> 00:08:51,509
[The decade-old OST revived by
the Moonlight Princes' voices]

209
00:08:51,509 --> 00:08:52,795
You're awesome!

210
00:08:55,122 --> 00:09:03,653
<i>♪ Like our memories that are fading away ♪</i>

211
00:09:03,653 --> 00:09:09,270
<i>♪ We're standing in the white mist ♪</i>

212
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:14,341
<i>♪ My sight of you is fading away ♪</i>

213
00:09:14,341 --> 00:09:20,225
<i>♪ The sight of your bright smile ♪</i>

214
00:09:20,225 --> 00:09:23,729
<i>♪ I'm afraid I'll forget it ♪</i>

215
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:30,470
<i>♪ I'd close my eyes, but I'd still see you ♪</i>

216
00:09:30,470 --> 00:09:37,290
<i>♪ Do you know what it feels like to miss you? ♪</i>

217
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:43,430
<i>♪ Beyond the misty road,
if you're searching for me ♪</i>

218
00:09:43,430 --> 00:09:44,937
Park Bo Gum!

219
00:09:44,937 --> 00:09:51,534
<i>♪ Would you follow the road
drawn by the moonlight? ♪</i>

220
00:09:51,534 --> 00:09:57,837
<i>♪ If only we could bloom the flowers
of springtime once more ♪</i>

221
00:09:57,837 --> 00:09:59,217
Jung Jin Young!

222
00:09:59,217 --> 00:10:07,330
<i>♪ If only we could go back,
of which I can only dream ♪</i>

223
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:12,132
We love you, Moonlight Princes!

224
00:10:18,990 --> 00:10:20,954
Bo Gum's tearing up.

225
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:29,637
<i>♪ With time inching away,
will our pain do the same? ♪</i>

226
00:10:29,637 --> 00:10:35,170
<i>♪ Will it fade like the mist? ♪</i>

227
00:10:35,170 --> 00:10:40,287
<i>♪ My memory of you is darkening ♪</i>

228
00:10:40,287 --> 00:10:46,097
<i>♪ The memory that I hold of you ♪</i>

229
00:10:46,097 --> 00:10:49,790
<i>♪ I'm afraid it'll disappear ♪</i>

230
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:56,441
<i>♪ I'd close my eyes, but I'd still see you ♪</i>

231
00:10:56,441 --> 00:11:03,030
<i>♪ Do you know what it feels like to miss you? ♪</i>

232
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:10,327
<i>♪ Beyond the misty road,
if you're searching for me ♪</i>

233
00:11:10,327 --> 00:11:17,483
<i>♪ Would you follow the road
drawn by the moonlight? ♪</i>

234
00:11:17,483 --> 00:11:25,154
<i>♪ If only we could bloom the flowers
of springtime once more ♪</i>

235
00:11:25,154 --> 00:11:32,510
<i>♪ If only we could go back,
of which I can only dream ♪</i>

236
00:11:32,510 --> 00:11:39,509
<i>♪ Even if I lost my sight,
and the world faded away ♪</i>

237
00:11:39,509 --> 00:11:46,166
<i>♪ Even if I closed my blurry eyes,
and tears spilled from them ♪</i>

238
00:11:46,166 --> 00:11:53,618
<i>♪ Someday, I will return to you,
standing in front of you ♪</i>

239
00:11:53,618 --> 00:12:02,391
<i>♪ It might not have been extravagant,
but our love was good ♪</i>

240
00:12:02,391 --> 00:12:08,455
<i>♪ Beyond the misty road,
if you're searching for me ♪</i>

241
00:12:08,455 --> 00:12:09,992
Where are you!

242
00:12:09,992 --> 00:12:16,643
<i>♪ Would you follow the road
drawn by the moonlight? ♪</i>

243
00:12:16,643 --> 00:12:24,247
<i>♪ If only we could bloom the flowers
of springtime once more ♪</i>

244
00:12:24,247 --> 00:12:32,071
<i>♪ If only we could go back,
of which I can only dream ♪</i>

245
00:12:32,071 --> 00:12:40,564
<i>♪ Like our memories that are fading away ♪</i>

246
00:12:40,564 --> 00:12:47,084
<i>♪ We're standing in the white mist ♪</i>

247
00:12:47,931 --> 00:12:51,362
[A stage that brought tears
to the Moonlight cast's eyes]

248
00:12:51,362 --> 00:12:52,944
Hey, what's up with you?

249
00:12:52,944 --> 00:12:54,262
Come on, don't cry.

250
00:12:54,262 --> 00:12:56,279
[Tearing up as well]

251
00:12:56,279 --> 00:12:58,971
Why'd you make her cry?

252
00:12:58,971 --> 00:13:01,188
[Their true efforts came through]
It was just a really good song.

253
00:13:01,188 --> 00:13:02,739
A really good song, huh?

254
00:13:02,739 --> 00:13:05,284
Reminded you of the good old days, didn't it?

255
00:13:05,284 --> 00:13:06,764
It was just so beautiful, the two of them.

256
00:13:07,798 --> 00:13:09,255
Thank you.

257
00:13:10,024 --> 00:13:12,629
[Host Bo Gum is back]
Well, Jin Young from 'Moonlight Princes,'

258
00:13:12,629 --> 00:13:14,306
- How did you like the performance?
- It was awesome!

259
00:13:14,306 --> 00:13:16,783
Where is Bo Gum from the Moonlight Princes?

260
00:13:16,783 --> 00:13:19,091
- Mr. Bo Gum!
- Come on, quick!

261
00:13:19,091 --> 00:13:20,751
[MC Bo Gum...]
Come on, quick!

262
00:13:20,751 --> 00:13:22,288
[Now Moonlight Prince Bo Gum]

263
00:13:22,288 --> 00:13:25,264
- Ah, yes, hello.
- They've got different personalities!

264
00:13:25,264 --> 00:13:26,575
Completely different.

265
00:13:26,575 --> 00:13:28,044
[He's shy, unlike MC Bo Gum]
Oh, he's an introvert.

266
00:13:28,044 --> 00:13:29,648
From what we've heard,

267
00:13:29,648 --> 00:13:33,091
- you played the piano for this version, right?
- That's correct.

268
00:13:33,091 --> 00:13:34,375
[Bo Gum worked the keys for this remix]
Yes, how did you know?

269
00:13:34,375 --> 00:13:36,678
Well, seeing how much
this project meant to me...

270
00:13:36,678 --> 00:13:38,415
I wanted to help however I could.

271
00:13:38,415 --> 00:13:41,052
[Bo Gum and Jin Young collaborated]
It was such an honor to work on it together.

272
00:13:41,052 --> 00:13:43,550
And, what you just heard will be released.

273
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:46,770
[It's been digitally released!]
It'll be available to stream.

274
00:13:46,770 --> 00:13:49,642
[Lots of love to the 2026 ver. of 'Misty Road']
Please look forward to it.

275
00:13:49,642 --> 00:13:53,059
But this isn't the end
of 'Moonlight Cantabile.'

276
00:13:53,059 --> 00:13:56,597
[Time to reminisce on decade-old memories]
This time, we'll look back on good memories...

277
00:13:56,597 --> 00:13:59,294
and really get to relive them, so to say.

278
00:13:59,294 --> 00:14:01,398
We have a special video ready for you.

279
00:14:01,398 --> 00:14:03,184
Now, let's watch it...

280
00:14:03,184 --> 00:14:05,095
- together!
- Together!

281
00:14:05,095 --> 00:14:07,713
[Setting up for the video]
Wow, but seriously...

282
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:09,522
- Why did you cry just now?
- Huh? Just now?

283
00:14:09,522 --> 00:14:10,782
Yeah, just wanted to know why.

284
00:14:10,782 --> 00:14:12,595
I was just watching them sing, right.

285
00:14:14,506 --> 00:14:17,143
And I could feel how genuine they were.

286
00:14:18,342 --> 00:14:19,793
See, I'm being genuine and vulnerable,

287
00:14:19,793 --> 00:14:21,435
and we're all here together
with genuine hearts, too.

288
00:14:21,435 --> 00:14:24,126
[The five friends are here for each other]
Like, making time for each other and gathering.

289
00:14:24,126 --> 00:14:26,790
So, seeing them standing there,
the two of them, singing like that...

290
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:29,294
[A performance, prepared with passion]
it's just a big deal, you know.

291
00:14:29,294 --> 00:14:31,658
They prepared it for us.

292
00:14:31,658 --> 00:14:34,526
[The sight of their performance...]
Just the fact that they gave it their all,

293
00:14:34,526 --> 00:14:37,905
[is enough to bring tears to her eyes]
was really making me tear up.

294
00:14:37,905 --> 00:14:40,528
I felt how sincere they were being.

295
00:14:40,528 --> 00:14:42,903
That's why I cried.

296
00:14:45,864 --> 00:14:49,615
[The decade-long friends
understand each other's true feelings]

297
00:14:49,615 --> 00:14:52,672
- Yeah, Bo Gum was tearing up, too.
- Exactly.

298
00:14:55,818 --> 00:15:00,778
[Best scenes chosen by the Moonlight Five]

299
00:15:00,778 --> 00:15:02,504
[Bo Gum, Prince Lee Yeong's pick]

300
00:15:02,504 --> 00:15:04,765
Oh, that's a cute shot.

301
00:15:04,765 --> 00:15:08,082
The moment I read
the script for that scene,

302
00:15:08,082 --> 00:15:10,319
I literally couldn't help
but scream from the excitement.

303
00:15:10,319 --> 00:15:12,576
[Which scene could have made him so giddy?]
It felt like I was in a manga, totally unreal.

304
00:15:12,576 --> 00:15:14,594
That moment, that scene, was so good.

305
00:15:15,711 --> 00:15:17,236
<i>So, then, Mr. Out-of-Touch.</i>

306
00:15:17,236 --> 00:15:18,774
<i>What's your actual name?</i>

307
00:15:18,774 --> 00:15:22,587
[The scene where Lee Yeong reveals his
royal background to the unsuspecting Sam Nom]

308
00:15:24,494 --> 00:15:25,669
<i>You.</i>

309
00:15:27,144 --> 00:15:29,328
<i>You asked me what my name is, correct?</i>

310
00:16:08,804 --> 00:16:10,748
[Bo Gum's chosen best scene]
<i>It's Lee Yeong.</i>

311
00:16:10,748 --> 00:16:12,751
["It's Lee Yeong, my name."]
<i>My name.</i>

312
00:16:15,753 --> 00:16:17,055
Oh, her face!

313
00:16:17,055 --> 00:16:18,986
"It's Lee Yeong, my name."

314
00:16:18,986 --> 00:16:21,684
That scene gave me chills just reading it.

315
00:16:21,684 --> 00:16:26,263
I imagine it wouldn't be easy to get a prince
to say his name out loud like that.

316
00:16:26,263 --> 00:16:28,807
I wanted to nail the scene. I really wanted to.

317
00:16:28,807 --> 00:16:32,686
I wanted it to become a fan-favorite.
A scene that anyone would fall in love with.

318
00:16:32,686 --> 00:16:35,786
So I'd practice making it bright and bubbly,
and then stern and serious, I tried everything.

319
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:39,723
[He wanted it to be perfect]
I tried out many variations on my own.

320
00:16:39,723 --> 00:16:43,442
Thinking back to it,
I still feel all soft and warm inside.

321
00:16:44,073 --> 00:16:47,409
<i>That's when I really started
to see how charismatic Bo Gum is.</i>

322
00:16:47,409 --> 00:16:51,204
<i>That's when I really started
to see how charismatic Bo Gum is.</i>

323
00:16:51,204 --> 00:16:52,935
[This voice...]

324
00:16:52,935 --> 00:16:55,793
- What?
- Oh, here's where he comes in.

325
00:16:55,793 --> 00:16:57,631
[Whose voice is making everyone smile so much?]
There he is.

326
00:16:57,631 --> 00:16:59,604
[Director Kim Seong Yoon]
The line, "It's Lee Yeong," is...

327
00:16:59,604 --> 00:17:02,257
where he reveals his true self.

328
00:17:02,257 --> 00:17:04,659
He's basically saying
that he's ready for romance.

329
00:17:04,659 --> 00:17:07,184
That's when I really saw it.

330
00:17:07,184 --> 00:17:10,907
It was as if Bo Gum
had actually become Prince Lee Yeong.

331
00:17:10,907 --> 00:17:13,811
There's this scene where
Prince Lee Yeong introduces himself.

332
00:17:13,811 --> 00:17:17,542
[Surprise!]
There's this scene where

333
00:17:17,542 --> 00:17:20,442
[Director of Photography, Kim Si Hyeong]
Prince Lee Yeong introduces himself.

334
00:17:20,442 --> 00:17:22,659
[Familiar faces all around]
It was so captivating.

335
00:17:22,659 --> 00:17:25,230
I think it's the first time
I've ever thought a guy was cool like that.

336
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:28,199
I could see his aura, just coming off of him.

337
00:17:28,199 --> 00:17:32,412
That's when I knew the show was going to
blow up, and of course, him as well.

338
00:17:32,412 --> 00:17:34,532
I do recall that it wasn't always easy.

339
00:17:34,532 --> 00:17:37,935
Lee Yeong and I are nothing alike, really.

340
00:17:37,935 --> 00:17:41,486
So it'd be hard to embody him sometimes.

341
00:17:41,486 --> 00:17:45,796
I remember feeling trapped,
and trying to break out of it.

342
00:17:45,796 --> 00:17:50,320
There was this scene in a hole,
with me and You Jung.

343
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:52,904
[Lee Yeong, tricked by Sam Nom,]
That scene, in the hole,

344
00:17:52,904 --> 00:17:54,515
[falls into a hole in the ground]
was a really important one.

345
00:17:54,515 --> 00:17:56,509
We had some trouble with the camera angle.

346
00:17:57,813 --> 00:17:58,981
<i>Ugh, seriously!</i>

347
00:17:58,981 --> 00:18:01,752
<i>Reach your arm further!</i>

348
00:18:01,752 --> 00:18:05,154
<i>Well, you should hoist me up higher!</i>

349
00:18:05,154 --> 00:18:06,584
"Hong Sam Nom, this is all because of you,"

350
00:18:06,584 --> 00:18:09,175
"now I'm stuck in this tiny, dirty space!"

351
00:18:09,175 --> 00:18:13,244
I tried to convey the explosive emotions
that he would've felt.

352
00:18:13,244 --> 00:18:17,148
Around sundown,
I guess Bo Gum also got frustrated...

353
00:18:17,148 --> 00:18:20,087
and started swearing,
but that was what made it so good.

354
00:18:20,087 --> 00:18:21,838
[Sam Nom escapes the hole first,]
<i>Sorry!</i>

355
00:18:21,838 --> 00:18:23,564
[and abandons Lee Yeong]
<i>I'm free!</i>

356
00:18:25,048 --> 00:18:26,758
<i>You insolent little bastard!</i>

357
00:18:26,758 --> 00:18:29,428
<i>You porking bowl of soup!</i>

358
00:18:29,428 --> 00:18:32,639
<i>Come back here right this instant!</i>

359
00:18:32,639 --> 00:18:37,620
I improvised "porking bowl of soup,"
that's how passionate I was.

360
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,689
I think that was my first improvised line ever.

361
00:18:40,689 --> 00:18:45,543
That was my biggest step towards
really becoming Lee Yeong as a character.

362
00:18:45,543 --> 00:18:49,184
My confidence sure peaked after that,
so the rest of the show was a breeze.

363
00:18:49,184 --> 00:18:52,395
Simply put, it was like Park Bo Gum was acting,

364
00:18:52,395 --> 00:18:54,432
until he was Prince Lee Yeong himself.

365
00:18:54,432 --> 00:18:57,166
And ever since then,
he could do whatever and it'd still be good.

366
00:18:58,244 --> 00:18:59,955
[The directors' words are like a pack of gifts]
That's awesome.

367
00:18:59,955 --> 00:19:02,899
- I didn't know they interviewed the directors.
- Yeah, I had no idea.

368
00:19:02,899 --> 00:19:06,340
I'm a little embarrassed,
hearing such flattering words.

369
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:08,926
"It's Lee Yeong." Oh, wait, that scene!

370
00:19:08,926 --> 00:19:11,496
Could you do it like,
"It's Park Bo Gum," for us?

371
00:19:11,496 --> 00:19:12,837
Into the camera.

372
00:19:12,837 --> 00:19:14,306
["It's Park Bo Gum. My name." in 2026!]
Just Park Bo Gum?

373
00:19:14,306 --> 00:19:15,306
Yeah, just into the camera.

374
00:19:16,393 --> 00:19:17,958
It's Park Bo Gum.

375
00:19:18,769 --> 00:19:20,326
My name.

376
00:19:21,424 --> 00:19:23,824
You know, he really does whatever he's told to.

377
00:19:23,824 --> 00:19:26,722
[School president Park never backs down!]
He really does.

378
00:19:26,722 --> 00:19:28,499
[You Jung's pick as Joseon's one and only
crossdressing eunuch Sam Nom, and Ra On]

379
00:19:28,499 --> 00:19:30,956
Oh, how adorable!

380
00:19:38,744 --> 00:19:40,088
[You Jung's choice of best scene
is 'Ra On's solo dance.']

381
00:19:40,088 --> 00:19:43,682
Yeah, this one.
This one's absolutely worthy of the title.

382
00:19:50,678 --> 00:19:53,748
This person, Ra On, was born a girl,

383
00:19:53,748 --> 00:19:56,606
but she never got to live a woman's life.

384
00:19:56,606 --> 00:20:00,451
So this scene is where
she finds solace in her dance.

385
00:20:00,451 --> 00:20:03,854
All her worries and obligations
that have been weighing on her,

386
00:20:03,854 --> 00:20:06,646
this is where she gets
a brief moment to be free of them.

387
00:20:06,646 --> 00:20:09,610
This scene is where she unfurls herself.

388
00:20:09,610 --> 00:20:12,360
But her eyes are still sorrowful,
because the act will come to an end.

389
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:13,851
She'll have to return to her shackles.

390
00:20:13,851 --> 00:20:16,328
And she can't let anyone
find out about her existence.

391
00:20:20,104 --> 00:20:22,569
<i>But Mother, you are the queen,</i>

392
00:20:22,569 --> 00:20:24,372
[Lee Yeong is reminded of his mother...]
<i>and I am a prince!</i>

393
00:20:24,372 --> 00:20:26,376
[from Ra On's dance]
<i>That's not always how things must be.</i>

394
00:20:26,376 --> 00:20:30,941
<i>There's no law that forbids us
from dancing barefoot in the rain.</i>

395
00:20:30,941 --> 00:20:33,591
I consider that scene to be an emotional one.

396
00:20:33,591 --> 00:20:38,495
Ra On's dance reminds
Lee Yeong of his mother, see.

397
00:20:38,495 --> 00:20:41,399
So, rather than just
making the dance look smooth,

398
00:20:41,399 --> 00:20:44,945
I wanted every movement to show emotion.

399
00:20:45,814 --> 00:20:49,028
Unfortunately, we shot that scene
on the hottest days of that summer.

400
00:20:49,028 --> 00:20:50,692
July 29th, 30th, and 31st.

401
00:20:50,692 --> 00:20:55,408
[He remembers the exact date?]
It must've been very hard on Ms. You Jung.

402
00:20:55,408 --> 00:20:57,623
She did swimmingly, though. It was perfect.

403
00:20:57,623 --> 00:20:59,743
Ms. You Jung, at the set, is like...

404
00:20:59,743 --> 00:21:01,204
Oh, I actually shouldn't call her that.

405
00:21:01,204 --> 00:21:02,800
I should call her "professor," or something.

406
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:05,249
[She's not just a Dr., but a professor now!]
<i>I should call her "professor," or something.</i>

407
00:21:05,249 --> 00:21:07,378
Professor You Jung is, well...

408
00:21:07,378 --> 00:21:08,679
Awe-inspiring.

409
00:21:08,679 --> 00:21:11,335
I would never be able to do
what she did at her young age.

410
00:21:11,335 --> 00:21:15,592
The sheer amount of effort
that goes into what she managed to do...

411
00:21:15,592 --> 00:21:18,142
[She was only seventeen!]
I don't know how she did it.

412
00:21:18,142 --> 00:21:22,726
She wouldn't even complain about it.
Now that's inspiring.

413
00:21:22,726 --> 00:21:24,603
When we were shooting that scene,

414
00:21:24,603 --> 00:21:26,855
[The hard times are coming back to mind]
I was only standing in the back, doing nothing.

415
00:21:26,855 --> 00:21:29,416
But I was still so hot and tired.

416
00:21:29,416 --> 00:21:33,153
["Professor" Kim You Jung, an inspiring sight]
Yet, you were dancing for days on end!

417
00:21:33,153 --> 00:21:37,242
- Yeah, you're right.
- The director must've been so touched, too.

418
00:21:37,242 --> 00:21:39,402
- He remembers the date!
- He remembers the exact dates, right!

419
00:21:39,402 --> 00:21:40,832
<i>July 29th, 30th, and 31st.</i>

420
00:21:40,832 --> 00:21:42,345
It's been 10 years, no less!

421
00:21:42,345 --> 00:21:44,539
- Yeah, it's no joke.
- He'd be so good at holding a grudge--

422
00:21:44,539 --> 00:21:46,792
[Too scared to finish his sentence]
He'd be so good at holding a grudge--

423
00:21:46,792 --> 00:21:50,009
[He's got such good memory]
A grudge!

424
00:21:50,009 --> 00:21:52,839
What I remember from that scene, though...

425
00:21:52,839 --> 00:21:57,348
[Bo Gum was so tired, he fell asleep]
is Bo Gum, dozing away from exhaustion.

426
00:21:57,348 --> 00:22:00,391
I felt so bad for him, really.

427
00:22:00,391 --> 00:22:02,768
He sat in that exact seat for three days!

428
00:22:02,768 --> 00:22:06,612
It went on all night.
But we three had day scenes together, too.

429
00:22:06,612 --> 00:22:08,498
[He had no time to rest]
So of course he was exhausted.

430
00:22:08,498 --> 00:22:10,148
He'd sort of fall asleep, like this...

431
00:22:10,148 --> 00:22:13,864
and jump awake at the word "Action!"

432
00:22:13,864 --> 00:22:16,238
I felt so sorry for him, seeing that.

433
00:22:16,238 --> 00:22:18,769
I look puffy in the scenes if you look closely.

434
00:22:18,769 --> 00:22:22,702
[His bloodshot eyes added to the scene]
See, look how tired he looks. Just look!

435
00:22:22,702 --> 00:22:24,057
That's what went on back then.

436
00:22:25,118 --> 00:22:27,631
[Dong Yeon, as Byeong Yeon
the lone warrior's pick]

437
00:22:27,631 --> 00:22:29,996
- He looks so cool!
- Very cool.

438
00:22:31,218 --> 00:22:35,404
[Scene where the imperial army
and the Baekwoon gang are fighting]

439
00:22:40,171 --> 00:22:45,191
[Byeong Yeon, knowing that he will
likely die for doing this,]

440
00:22:45,191 --> 00:22:49,622
[still threatens Lee Yeong
to protect Lee Yeong and Ra On]

441
00:22:49,622 --> 00:22:52,358
[Dong Yeon's best scene is...]
<i>If you want the prince alive, hear, all of you!</i>

442
00:22:52,358 --> 00:22:56,838
['Byeong Yeon threatening Lee Yeong']

443
00:22:57,529 --> 00:22:59,158
<i>Stow your blades.</i>

444
00:23:03,118 --> 00:23:04,503
<i>Byeong Yeon...</i>

445
00:23:09,334 --> 00:23:10,837
<i>Do not put that blade away.</i>

446
00:23:13,587 --> 00:23:15,648
<i>The moment you do...</i>

447
00:23:18,176 --> 00:23:20,039
<i>I'll lose you.</i>

448
00:23:29,849 --> 00:23:31,330
<i>No!</i>

449
00:23:38,851 --> 00:23:40,108
<i>Byeong Yeon!</i>

450
00:23:46,384 --> 00:23:47,669
<i>Hey, Byeong Yeon...</i>

451
00:23:52,278 --> 00:23:53,907
<i>I...</i>

452
00:23:58,798 --> 00:24:00,606
<i>thank you...</i>

453
00:24:07,851 --> 00:24:09,429
<i>for trusting me.</i>

454
00:24:15,474 --> 00:24:21,108
See, we, Kwak Dong Yeon and Park Bo Gum,
have already become such good friends by then.

455
00:24:21,108 --> 00:24:25,242
And shooting this scene after
we've already established a true connection,

456
00:24:25,242 --> 00:24:29,861
[The actors and characters are both friends]
we had the same kind of relationship...

457
00:24:29,861 --> 00:24:32,457
that the characters would have, you see.

458
00:24:32,457 --> 00:24:36,378
Bo Gum was actually heartbroken
when we shot that scene.

459
00:24:36,378 --> 00:24:39,548
And it hurt me to see him so hurt.

460
00:24:39,548 --> 00:24:42,978
It all felt so human, you know.
I put my real emotions through.

461
00:24:42,978 --> 00:24:46,392
Of course, when you work together,
you bond with each other.

462
00:24:46,392 --> 00:24:50,280
So the characters become
more and more well-fitted.

463
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:53,144
I think that's what made
that scene so devastating.

464
00:24:53,144 --> 00:24:55,600
I was just so determined.

465
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:57,052
I wanted to make it happen.

466
00:24:57,052 --> 00:25:01,486
Byeong Yeon would've carried
his sword around for all of his life.

467
00:25:01,486 --> 00:25:04,197
So, how would he position himself when he sits?

468
00:25:04,197 --> 00:25:07,511
That's the kind of question I asked myself.
To give it that last bit of realism.

469
00:25:07,511 --> 00:25:08,666
But how would I know?

470
00:25:08,666 --> 00:25:13,535
So I carried my sword all the way
from Cheongdam to Nonhyeon every day.

471
00:25:13,535 --> 00:25:15,250
It was my fake practice sword, of course.

472
00:25:15,250 --> 00:25:18,246
I'd think, "he'd have calloused hands,"

473
00:25:18,246 --> 00:25:21,223
so I'd keep rubbing my hands
to make them rougher.

474
00:25:21,223 --> 00:25:23,668
I wanted to impress Director Kim Seong Yoon.

475
00:25:23,668 --> 00:25:27,475
We know each other pretty well,
and of course we're close.

476
00:25:27,475 --> 00:25:29,472
So it was all the more reason
to not let him down.

477
00:25:29,472 --> 00:25:32,805
I felt obliged to impress him, basically.

478
00:25:33,602 --> 00:25:37,171
I first met Kwak Dong Yeon when he was 17,
when we worked on 'Puberty Medley,'

479
00:25:37,171 --> 00:25:39,380
and he has never let me down once.

480
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:40,942
Not even once.

481
00:25:40,942 --> 00:25:45,065
I think he's just meant to be an actor.

482
00:25:46,351 --> 00:25:49,635
I think he's just meant to be an actor.

483
00:25:51,328 --> 00:25:54,080
- That's the best compliment an actor can get.
- Yeah, true.

484
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:56,066
- "Never let me down, not even once..."
- So true.

485
00:25:56,066 --> 00:25:57,496
He could be lying.

486
00:25:57,496 --> 00:25:59,419
[He's so flustered!]

487
00:25:59,419 --> 00:26:02,404
[I'll treasure this video]
Can I have a copy of that clip?

488
00:26:02,404 --> 00:26:05,015
If you think about it now,

489
00:26:05,015 --> 00:26:08,426
it's really not common to see friendship...

490
00:26:08,426 --> 00:26:12,495
[A complex character...]
conveyed in such an intricate way.

491
00:26:12,495 --> 00:26:14,392
[forced to betray a beloved friend]
It's rare to see.

492
00:26:14,392 --> 00:26:16,645
Looking back, if it weren't for Bo Gum,

493
00:26:16,645 --> 00:26:21,024
I don't think I would've been able
to get such a good grasp on my role.

494
00:26:21,024 --> 00:26:24,665
[The two were influential to each other]
Well, Dong Yeon made me very happy back then.

495
00:26:24,665 --> 00:26:27,076
One day, when there's more time behind us,

496
00:26:27,076 --> 00:26:29,940
I'd love to co-star with you again
on something completely new.

497
00:26:29,940 --> 00:26:32,469
- I want to work with you guys again.
- That would be nice.

498
00:26:32,469 --> 00:26:35,988
- How about a sitcom?
- Maybe that would be for the best, yeah.

499
00:26:35,988 --> 00:26:37,791
[Jin Young, the handsome scholar's pick]

500
00:26:37,791 --> 00:26:40,428
- Look how fair he is.
- Pretty as a daisy.

501
00:26:40,428 --> 00:26:50,296
[Yoon Seong breaks the door
to save Lee Yeong and Ra On]

502
00:27:04,701 --> 00:27:06,128
What a real man he is!

503
00:27:06,128 --> 00:27:10,032
[Jin Young's choice is
'Yoon Seong stopping a blade with his hand']

504
00:27:10,032 --> 00:27:14,009
I had never been in a martial arts act
with swords before,

505
00:27:14,009 --> 00:27:15,486
so I was quite nervous.

506
00:27:15,486 --> 00:27:19,916
It's the type of act where one awkward move
can sour the whole scene.

507
00:27:19,916 --> 00:27:22,195
I tried really hard not to screw it up.

508
00:27:23,002 --> 00:27:27,139
Out of all my scenes, that one's my favorite.

509
00:27:27,139 --> 00:27:28,216
He's so cute.

510
00:27:28,216 --> 00:27:30,413
I rewatched it myself a few times, actually.

511
00:27:30,413 --> 00:27:34,073
[Folded under no pressure]
I rewatched it myself a few times, actually.

512
00:27:34,681 --> 00:27:35,996
[My precious best scene!]
He's adorable.

513
00:27:35,996 --> 00:27:37,392
<i>We ran on a very tight schedule...</i>

514
00:27:37,392 --> 00:27:39,706
- Oh, what?
<i>- so from what I remember,</i>

515
00:27:39,706 --> 00:27:41,910
[Director Kang Soo Yeon]
We ran on a very tight schedule...

516
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:46,526
so from what I remember, I doubt he had time
to go to an action school.

517
00:27:46,526 --> 00:27:50,518
He had deadlines to meet,
but he still met all our expectations.

518
00:27:50,518 --> 00:27:53,324
He's such a fast learner
when it comes to action.

519
00:27:53,324 --> 00:27:56,161
That's what he's capable of,
and that capability is everything.

520
00:27:56,161 --> 00:27:57,821
Maybe it's because he dances a lot,

521
00:27:57,821 --> 00:28:02,292
like, all that dancing must've helped him,
or at least I think that's why.

522
00:28:02,292 --> 00:28:04,421
Anyway, that ability to sync well
is an admirable trait.

523
00:28:04,421 --> 00:28:06,817
It helps us do our job, too.

524
00:28:06,817 --> 00:28:08,365
I get what she means.

525
00:28:08,365 --> 00:28:11,295
[His martial arts practice was dance]
It's clear that you're adept with your body.

526
00:28:11,295 --> 00:28:12,460
[Flustered]
Oh, you think so?

527
00:28:12,460 --> 00:28:15,114
Wait, how many times have you rewatched it?

528
00:28:15,114 --> 00:28:17,557
Do you still do it sometimes?

529
00:28:17,557 --> 00:28:20,264
- Yeah, I guess I have recently.
- Really?

530
00:28:20,264 --> 00:28:22,187
Really?

531
00:28:22,187 --> 00:28:25,384
But, hear me out,
I was really proud of that scene.

532
00:28:25,384 --> 00:28:26,399
[Still has more to say]
In fact...

533
00:28:26,399 --> 00:28:28,777
[That's where the highlight starts]
it's the part where I smash the door in.

534
00:28:28,777 --> 00:28:30,236
Oh, the part where you roll in?

535
00:28:30,236 --> 00:28:31,269
[Coolest entry ever!]

536
00:28:31,928 --> 00:28:36,041
[Duck, roll, kablam, perfect slice!]

537
00:28:36,041 --> 00:28:37,285
[Full of charisma]

538
00:28:37,285 --> 00:28:40,308
That's where I start watching from.

539
00:28:40,308 --> 00:28:42,712
[Can't miss out on my best scene!]
That's where it gets really intense, you know.

540
00:28:42,712 --> 00:28:45,856
[How is our eldest so darn cute?]

541
00:28:45,856 --> 00:28:48,171
[Soo Bin, the Snow White maiden's best scene]

542
00:28:48,171 --> 00:28:49,735
Let's see.

543
00:28:51,109 --> 00:28:53,965
The character Ha Yeon that I remember,

544
00:28:53,965 --> 00:28:57,828
is someone who isn't held back
by the social oppression of the Joseon era.

545
00:28:57,828 --> 00:29:03,996
[Which scene did she choose from her role?]
She's a go-getter, a strong, progressive woman.

546
00:29:04,748 --> 00:29:06,940
[Ha Yeon, finding out
that Lee Yeong loves Ra On,]

547
00:29:06,940 --> 00:29:09,979
[resigns from her role as the crown princess]
<i>Your Highness, I knew it all along.</i>

548
00:29:09,979 --> 00:29:12,387
<i>I knew you didn't love me.</i>

549
00:29:17,806 --> 00:29:19,077
[Soo Bin's pick is 'Ha Yeon's fresh new start']

550
00:29:19,077 --> 00:29:21,317
At the finale, she takes off her outer cover.

551
00:29:21,317 --> 00:29:25,888
She seems so free, and so relieved, even,
and that scene really stuck with me.

552
00:29:31,141 --> 00:29:33,245
<i>The sun is beautiful today.</i>

553
00:29:34,050 --> 00:29:36,442
<i>- Let's go.
- Yes, my lady.</i>

554
00:29:37,681 --> 00:29:39,931
The most common trope of a female sub-lead

555
00:29:39,931 --> 00:29:42,618
usually ends in her getting jealous
and trying to ruin others' relationships.

556
00:29:42,618 --> 00:29:44,900
But that's not what Ha Yeon was like.

557
00:29:44,900 --> 00:29:47,124
She's very honest
and unafraid to speak her mind.

558
00:29:47,124 --> 00:29:49,533
And even when she does get jealous,

559
00:29:49,533 --> 00:29:52,696
she's startled by this foreign feeling.

560
00:29:52,696 --> 00:29:55,373
But, in the end, she learns to embrace it.

561
00:29:55,373 --> 00:29:58,283
"Yes, I'm going to find my own life."

562
00:29:58,283 --> 00:30:02,875
I must've been impressed by that
image of a modern woman.

563
00:30:02,875 --> 00:30:06,011
[Director Kim Seong Yoon]
Soo Bin was already a rising star then,

564
00:30:06,011 --> 00:30:08,352
so I asked, "Would you play Ha Yeon?"

565
00:30:08,352 --> 00:30:10,107
She agreed to do it willingly.

566
00:30:10,107 --> 00:30:12,303
Even though she didn't have
a lot of screen time,

567
00:30:12,303 --> 00:30:14,678
she had already become Ha Yeon
in the afternoon scene.

568
00:30:16,049 --> 00:30:21,852
She's a friend with a lot of worries,
but I'm not worried about her.

569
00:30:21,852 --> 00:30:26,318
Should I say she's the kind of person
I want to be like?

570
00:30:26,318 --> 00:30:27,371
What?

571
00:30:27,371 --> 00:30:30,435
I was only 17 or 18 at the time.

572
00:30:30,435 --> 00:30:34,151
I expressed things very spontaneously.

573
00:30:34,151 --> 00:30:37,642
But the Soo Bin I saw was calm, quiet,

574
00:30:37,642 --> 00:30:41,352
and very composed, I would say.

575
00:30:41,352 --> 00:30:45,635
I thought back then that I wanted to be
like her when I became an adult.

576
00:30:46,256 --> 00:30:50,836
Watching these scenes and listening
to everyone talk,

577
00:30:50,836 --> 00:30:53,431
I feel a bit of regret, on one hand.

578
00:30:53,431 --> 00:30:58,356
Since I made my first appearance in Episode 5,

579
00:30:58,356 --> 00:31:01,259
I felt like a transfer student.

580
00:31:01,259 --> 00:31:04,169
I feel a bit sad now that I couldn't
be with everyone during those times.

581
00:31:04,169 --> 00:31:07,197
I think that's how I feel now.

582
00:31:07,197 --> 00:31:09,347
But on the other hand, I'm so relieved.

583
00:31:09,347 --> 00:31:15,640
I'm glad I gained such good people
who always remember and care for me.

584
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,281
She even said she wanted to be like you.

585
00:31:17,281 --> 00:31:18,522
Did you know she felt that way?

586
00:31:18,522 --> 00:31:22,967
[Admiration heard after 10 years]
I had no idea. My image is so different now.

587
00:31:22,967 --> 00:31:25,642
Actually, you were just being shy.

588
00:31:25,642 --> 00:31:30,054
- So I was completely mistaken.
- You were mistaken.

589
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:33,570
But I like the Soo Bin of now better.

590
00:31:33,570 --> 00:31:38,222
We saw each other all the time,
so we couldn't help but become close.

591
00:31:38,222 --> 00:31:41,519
Whenever we gathered, it was like a classroom.

592
00:31:41,519 --> 00:31:42,920
A school class.

593
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:46,978
Friendships with high school friends

594
00:31:46,978 --> 00:31:50,568
tend to last longer than those
made in the professional world.

595
00:31:50,568 --> 00:31:52,530
That's how Gurmi feels to me now.

596
00:31:52,530 --> 00:31:55,580
We really joked around a lot.

597
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:58,590
We'd laugh and cause so many bloopers
that the director scolded us.

598
00:31:58,590 --> 00:31:59,744
It happened a lot.

599
00:31:59,744 --> 00:32:04,574
We'd laugh at the most ridiculous things
and cause bloopers.

600
00:32:05,183 --> 00:32:07,900
By the second half, the set was so noisy.

601
00:32:07,900 --> 00:32:12,115
We'd be preparing to shoot,
but the noise was just...

602
00:32:13,065 --> 00:32:15,946
"Hurry up and get over here!"

603
00:32:15,946 --> 00:32:19,130
But it was cute to see them
shuffling over to do their part.

604
00:32:19,130 --> 00:32:21,652
I'd be annoyed, then find them cute again.

605
00:32:21,652 --> 00:32:24,049
I think that cycle just kept repeating.

606
00:32:24,049 --> 00:32:25,415
<i>Because they were so noisy.</i>

607
00:32:26,556 --> 00:32:28,352
They were just too noisy.

608
00:32:28,352 --> 00:32:30,150
[Who was so noisy?]
All of them.

609
00:32:30,150 --> 00:32:34,258
Starting with You Jung,
then Bo Gum and Dong Yeon. All of them.

610
00:32:34,258 --> 00:32:37,235
Staying up all night
with mosquitoes wears you out.

611
00:32:37,235 --> 00:32:42,427
Normally, you'd go rest in the car,
but they'd keep chatting all night.

612
00:32:42,427 --> 00:32:44,297
[Makeup Director Park Jin A]
It was really hot.

613
00:32:44,297 --> 00:32:47,472
There were record-breaking heat waves
one after another.

614
00:32:47,472 --> 00:32:51,369
The way these guys acted on set was so lovely.

615
00:32:51,369 --> 00:32:54,913
They even called each and every one of
the junior staff members by their names.

616
00:32:54,913 --> 00:32:57,662
If someone was carrying heavy things,
they'd help them out.

617
00:32:57,662 --> 00:33:00,278
[Costume Director Lee Jin Hee]
Actually, it was really tough.

618
00:33:00,278 --> 00:33:03,588
At that time,
we kept getting side scripts every day.

619
00:33:03,588 --> 00:33:07,095
The schedule was to stay up every single night.

620
00:33:07,095 --> 00:33:12,515
Despite that, maybe because
the actors were so young and vibrant...

621
00:33:12,515 --> 00:33:17,000
I think everyone fed off that energy
and endured that difficult set.

622
00:33:17,782 --> 00:33:20,464
- What was so funny back then?
- I know, right?

623
00:33:20,464 --> 00:33:24,958
I think we laughed a lot
during the chicken soup scene.

624
00:33:24,958 --> 00:33:28,457
- We hadn't slept for days then.
- Was that it?

625
00:33:28,457 --> 00:33:32,550
So all three of us were a bit out of it.

626
00:33:32,550 --> 00:33:34,885
We really got scolded back then.

627
00:33:34,885 --> 00:33:35,994
That's right. You're right.

628
00:33:35,994 --> 00:33:38,763
At first, they laughed along with us
like you just did.

629
00:33:38,763 --> 00:33:42,634
They tried to move on a few times, but...

630
00:33:42,634 --> 00:33:44,127
"Hey, what's so funny?"

631
00:33:45,836 --> 00:33:48,525
[The Jahyeondang Trio got scolded]
"Is this funny to you right now?"

632
00:33:48,525 --> 00:33:51,142
But above all,
the set was so fun and wonderful.

633
00:33:51,142 --> 00:33:52,317
- Exactly.
- It was.

634
00:33:52,317 --> 00:33:54,839
Being with good friends, good people,
and a great staff...

635
00:33:54,839 --> 00:33:57,634
Just being on that set together...

636
00:33:57,634 --> 00:34:00,812
Back then, it felt like it would last forever.

637
00:34:00,812 --> 00:34:04,292
[10 years have passed and become memories]
That's how the set felt.

638
00:34:05,429 --> 00:34:08,653
<i>Hi, guys! Hello, friends.</i>

639
00:34:08,653 --> 00:34:12,063
[Lee Jun Hyeok as Eunuch Jang]
Hi, guys! Hello, friends.

640
00:34:12,063 --> 00:34:13,364
How have you been?

641
00:34:13,364 --> 00:34:16,586
I can't believe it's already been ten years.

642
00:34:16,586 --> 00:34:18,817
It was such a happy time.

643
00:34:18,817 --> 00:34:21,004
Whether things are hard or you're happy,

644
00:34:21,004 --> 00:34:25,602
I'll be cheering you on from behind,
so please reach out.

645
00:34:25,602 --> 00:34:27,230
- Fighting!
- Fighting!

646
00:34:27,230 --> 00:34:29,020
[Jang Kwang as Han Sang Ik]
- Congratulations. - Sir!

647
00:34:29,020 --> 00:34:35,667
I hope you work harder, stay humble,
and grow into global stars.

648
00:34:35,667 --> 00:34:38,883
[Kim Seung Su as the King]
Are you guys having fun on your trip?

649
00:34:38,883 --> 00:34:42,173
- Dad!
- I'm jealous. Going just by yourselves.

650
00:34:42,173 --> 00:34:44,982
You all worked so hard in the middle of summer.

651
00:34:44,982 --> 00:34:47,765
The result of all that hard work

652
00:34:47,765 --> 00:34:52,296
is this chance to celebrate
our tenth anniversary like this.

653
00:34:52,296 --> 00:34:55,699
I'm proud as a father and a senior actor.

654
00:34:55,699 --> 00:34:58,929
Have fun. Have enough fun for me, too.

655
00:34:58,929 --> 00:35:01,023
Yes, thank you.

656
00:35:01,023 --> 00:35:04,548
The tenth anniversary is meaningful,
but for me...

657
00:35:04,548 --> 00:35:08,770
There's a sense of security
that ten years brings.

658
00:35:08,770 --> 00:35:13,184
Seeing you settled, relying on each other,
and having a tight bond...

659
00:35:13,184 --> 00:35:17,127
That kind of affection gives
me a greater sense of relief.

660
00:35:17,127 --> 00:35:19,724
I'm so grateful and proud of you all.

661
00:35:19,724 --> 00:35:25,498
I hope you continue to rely on each other
and live well together.

662
00:35:25,498 --> 00:35:27,483
I'm so proud and grateful.

663
00:35:27,483 --> 00:35:28,578
Goodbye.

664
00:35:29,633 --> 00:35:31,869
[Thank you]

665
00:35:31,869 --> 00:35:38,262
[Just like when we flew sky lanterns]
<i>Please make our Crown Prince's wish come true!</i>

666
00:35:40,097 --> 00:35:44,683
[Today, they write messages to each other]

667
00:35:46,185 --> 00:35:50,722
[Carefully writing down unspoken words]

668
00:35:52,953 --> 00:35:56,186
- Done.
- I'm finished.

669
00:35:58,428 --> 00:36:00,518
[Yoon Seong, thank you for protecting Ra On]

670
00:36:00,518 --> 00:36:03,287
[Prior engagements come first.
Let's be together next time]

671
00:36:03,287 --> 00:36:06,638
[I learned a lot from that teenage girl]

672
00:36:06,638 --> 00:36:10,142
[Now we'll protect you too]

673
00:36:10,142 --> 00:36:11,780
[Stay healthy]

674
00:36:11,780 --> 00:36:13,395
[Love you]

675
00:36:13,395 --> 00:36:14,760
[Together forever]

676
00:36:14,760 --> 00:36:16,580
[Thanks]

677
00:36:16,580 --> 00:36:22,386
We hope we can be friends forever.

678
00:36:22,386 --> 00:36:25,456
[Hoping for the Gurmi's eternal friendship]
- Thank you. - Thank you.

679
00:36:25,456 --> 00:36:28,818
[Sending up their wishes together]
- Thank you. - Thank you.

680
00:36:31,407 --> 00:36:33,117
I really hope it reaches the sky.

681
00:36:33,117 --> 00:36:35,377
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

682
00:36:35,987 --> 00:36:37,567
Thank you.

683
00:36:39,451 --> 00:36:42,893
[The Gurmi returns to the lodge]
Back to the lodge.

684
00:36:43,973 --> 00:36:46,362
There's something else here.

685
00:36:46,362 --> 00:36:48,093
- What is it?
- What's that?

686
00:36:48,093 --> 00:36:50,961
- It looks like a gift.
- But there are four of them.

687
00:36:50,961 --> 00:36:53,237
[Mysterious bundles]
- You're right. - What's this?

688
00:36:53,237 --> 00:36:56,294
- Shall we open them?
- These are gifts I prepared.

689
00:36:56,294 --> 00:36:57,735
- Really?
- For real?

690
00:36:57,735 --> 00:36:59,564
[A gift from You Jung]
- Yes. - What is it?

691
00:36:59,564 --> 00:37:02,177
- This is for Jin Young. This is for you.
- What?

692
00:37:02,177 --> 00:37:03,317
Really?

693
00:37:03,317 --> 00:37:06,444
[What could You Jung's gift be?]
- Seriously. - I wondered why there were four.

694
00:37:06,444 --> 00:37:09,008
What? Our names are on them.

695
00:37:09,008 --> 00:37:11,973
[Names from Love in the Moonlight]
It's definitely You Jung's handwriting.

696
00:37:12,923 --> 00:37:16,543
[Special custom pajamas for the team]
- I made them. - No way!

697
00:37:16,543 --> 00:37:18,029
What? What's on the back?

698
00:37:18,029 --> 00:37:20,924
[Drawings by You Jung on the back]
- There's a drawing. - What is it?

699
00:37:20,924 --> 00:37:22,406
- Did you draw this?
- Yes.

700
00:37:22,406 --> 00:37:26,008
- Based on your zodiac signs.
- Yes, I looked up everyone's signs.

701
00:37:26,640 --> 00:37:29,561
Jin Young is a Sheep and I'm an Ox.

702
00:37:29,561 --> 00:37:31,737
You Jung is a Rabbit, Bo Gum is a Rooster.

703
00:37:31,737 --> 00:37:34,011
[Deeply touched]
- Isn't it cute? - This is amazing.

704
00:37:34,011 --> 00:37:36,814
"Clouds Drawn by Love."
When did she draw all this?

705
00:37:36,814 --> 00:37:39,970
- It's so cute.
- Even while she was so busy.

706
00:37:39,970 --> 00:37:42,364
- I'll wash up and wear this to bed.
- Me too.

707
00:37:42,364 --> 00:37:43,944
Me too.

708
00:37:44,600 --> 00:37:48,373
[A night too precious to just sleep]
- It's a waste to just sleep. - Want to join?

709
00:37:48,373 --> 00:37:50,435
[The team gathers in pajamas]
Shall we have a toast?

710
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:51,923
Cheers.

711
00:37:51,923 --> 00:37:53,311
Cheers!

712
00:37:53,311 --> 00:37:54,678
Cheers!

713
00:37:55,847 --> 00:37:58,650
[Quenching their thirst with their favorites]

714
00:37:59,449 --> 00:38:02,741
[You Jung brings ice cream and snacks]
- Looks delicious. - At 2:00 a.m.

715
00:38:02,741 --> 00:38:04,795
I think it'll be good
if you put it on top of this.

716
00:38:04,795 --> 00:38:07,223
- That looks good.
- It is.

717
00:38:08,313 --> 00:38:10,928
- That looks good.
- It is.

718
00:38:10,928 --> 00:38:12,829
[Bo Gum joins in immediately]

719
00:38:14,833 --> 00:38:16,767
He's going all out.

720
00:38:17,769 --> 00:38:19,668
[Takes a bite of ice cream right away]
Really?

721
00:38:20,864 --> 00:38:22,893
Look at him enjoying it again.

722
00:38:22,893 --> 00:38:24,715
Should I put this on top?

723
00:38:24,715 --> 00:38:27,560
[Takes a bite of ice cream with a snack]
Didn't we use to do that?

724
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:30,099
- This is so good.
- I think we used to call each other at dawn.

725
00:38:30,099 --> 00:38:31,719
Isn't this amazing?

726
00:38:33,049 --> 00:38:34,438
I can't resist.

727
00:38:34,438 --> 00:38:37,053
[Dong Yeon joins the ice cream and snack combo]
Oh, what the heck.

728
00:38:37,053 --> 00:38:39,257
[Takes a bite immediately]

729
00:38:39,257 --> 00:38:42,151
- I think we used to call each other at dawn.
- Isn't this amazing?

730
00:38:46,484 --> 00:38:48,973
[A sound from an empty room?]

731
00:38:48,973 --> 00:38:50,667
Wait a minute.

732
00:38:50,667 --> 00:38:52,702
[What was that sound?]
Wait a minute.

733
00:38:53,738 --> 00:38:55,839
- That sound came from over there, right?
- Yeah.

734
00:38:55,839 --> 00:38:59,349
[In the room where the mysterious sound came]
Go check it out. You go.

735
00:38:59,945 --> 00:39:03,243
[Mannequins were moved here to avoid the dew]

736
00:39:03,243 --> 00:39:06,616
- Things like that appear in dreams. Seriously.
- In dreams?

737
00:39:08,093 --> 00:39:09,819
You scared me.

738
00:39:11,167 --> 00:39:12,668
You scared me.

739
00:39:12,668 --> 00:39:14,739
[Possessed by a mannequin ghost]
My back was itchy.

740
00:39:14,739 --> 00:39:17,161
Are you doing a robot dance?

741
00:39:17,161 --> 00:39:19,069
Boombastic. I think it's Boombastic.

742
00:39:19,069 --> 00:39:21,727
[Boombastic zombie resurrected after 10 years]
Boombastic.

743
00:39:22,534 --> 00:39:24,013
I came out to drink some water...

744
00:39:24,929 --> 00:39:26,430
And it's out here.

745
00:39:26,430 --> 00:39:29,414
You know this, right? Ice cream and cola.

746
00:39:29,414 --> 00:39:31,342
The one where it spews out?

747
00:39:31,342 --> 00:39:33,289
[For the ice cream and cola]
Let's do it.

748
00:39:33,289 --> 00:39:36,559
- Rock-paper-scissors.
- Rock-paper-scissors.

749
00:39:37,195 --> 00:39:38,798
[You Jung, Soo Bin, and Dong Yeon lose]

750
00:39:38,798 --> 00:39:40,624
I really don't want to do this.

751
00:39:40,624 --> 00:39:41,892
I really don't want to do this.

752
00:39:41,892 --> 00:39:44,167
[The losers face off again]
Rock-paper-scissors!

753
00:39:47,363 --> 00:39:49,820
[Soo Bin is chosen to eat ice cream and cola]

754
00:39:49,820 --> 00:39:50,835
I don't want to do it.

755
00:39:51,741 --> 00:39:53,911
[Heading to the kitchen
for cola faster than anyone]

756
00:39:53,911 --> 00:39:56,586
[United in purpose at times like this]
- Is there cola? - There is.

757
00:39:57,574 --> 00:39:59,357
[Cola delivered for the experiment]
Who suggested this?

758
00:39:59,357 --> 00:40:00,804
It was you.

759
00:40:00,804 --> 00:40:03,653
But where do I spit it? If I have to.

760
00:40:04,327 --> 00:40:06,308
At either of the guys.

761
00:40:06,308 --> 00:40:09,063
- You're the closest.
- This side is closer, actually.

762
00:40:09,063 --> 00:40:12,262
[The Gurmi's great friendship]
But the direction of the guys is better.

763
00:40:12,262 --> 00:40:13,524
[Eating the ice cream first]

764
00:40:13,524 --> 00:40:15,163
- Right away, before it melts.
- Right.

765
00:40:15,163 --> 00:40:16,888
[Taking a swig of cola]
Drink it and wait.

766
00:40:22,050 --> 00:40:26,749
[What will be the result of this experiment?]

767
00:40:30,435 --> 00:40:32,099
[Bubble, bubble up]

768
00:40:32,099 --> 00:40:33,933
[Dong Yeon is the chosen one]

769
00:40:33,933 --> 00:40:37,342
[Eating ice cream and cola together
really makes you spit it out]

770
00:40:37,342 --> 00:40:41,317
[Satisfied with the successful experiment]

771
00:40:45,207 --> 00:40:46,362
It fizzes up, right?

772
00:40:47,677 --> 00:40:48,959
Does it swell up suddenly?

773
00:40:48,959 --> 00:40:51,848
I thought I was okay,
but it started bubbling in my mouth.

774
00:40:54,323 --> 00:40:56,934
[The youngest helps clean up anyway]
That's fascinating.

775
00:40:56,934 --> 00:40:59,887
[The midnight commotion comes to an end]

776
00:40:59,887 --> 00:41:02,024
[Getting ready for bed]
I need to brush my teeth now.

777
00:41:06,792 --> 00:41:09,826
[Wandering around
with a toothbrush in his mouth]

778
00:41:09,826 --> 00:41:12,143
[Gathering in the living room one by one]

779
00:41:12,143 --> 00:41:16,547
It's so funny how we're all
in the living room brushing our teeth.

780
00:41:16,547 --> 00:41:19,048
We're like a bunch of zombies.

781
00:41:19,048 --> 00:41:22,186
[A tight-knit group of zombies]
Zombies.

782
00:41:22,186 --> 00:41:25,762
[The first day ends on a happy note]
- Good night. - Sleep well.

783
00:41:26,409 --> 00:41:30,117
[The morning of the second day arrives]

784
00:41:33,543 --> 00:41:36,777
[You Jung is the first to wake up]

785
00:41:36,777 --> 00:41:39,652
[Filling a pot with water
as soon as she wakes up]

786
00:41:40,444 --> 00:41:44,426
[Adding a whole lot of ice]

787
00:41:44,426 --> 00:41:45,884
[Tying her hair back tightly]

788
00:41:47,340 --> 00:41:51,354
[Dunking her face into the ice water]

789
00:41:56,712 --> 00:42:00,730
[Dunking it once more]

790
00:42:01,369 --> 00:42:04,312
[Shakes head side to side]

791
00:42:04,312 --> 00:42:08,911
[You Jung's refreshing morning routine ends]

792
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:13,806
[Everyone is finally awake]
What's for breakfast today?

793
00:42:13,806 --> 00:42:15,546
For breakfast today,

794
00:42:16,206 --> 00:42:19,323
- Tomato pasta.
- Oh, yes!

795
00:42:19,323 --> 00:42:20,500
Wait a second.

796
00:42:20,500 --> 00:42:24,734
- And pancakes and jam.
- Oh, yeah!

797
00:42:24,734 --> 00:42:28,627
- I'll make the pasta.
- I'll make the pancakes.

798
00:42:28,627 --> 00:42:31,754
[Soo Bin and Jin Young make pancake batter]
- You're good at stirring. - Right?

799
00:42:31,754 --> 00:42:33,543
Want to try making one first?

800
00:42:34,190 --> 00:42:36,493
<i>♪ Ding-a-ling-a-ling ♪</i>

801
00:42:39,945 --> 00:42:43,206
[Pouring the batter while humming]

802
00:42:43,836 --> 00:42:46,684
[A rather dainty size for a pancake]
Is this too thin?

803
00:42:46,684 --> 00:42:48,392
[Let's see]

804
00:42:52,055 --> 00:42:54,011
[He can't flip it and just pokes at it]

805
00:42:54,011 --> 00:42:55,494
This is so scary.

806
00:42:56,277 --> 00:42:59,367
[Bo Gum's pancake is clumsily finished]
As for the rest...

807
00:43:00,349 --> 00:43:02,925
This case is a bit complicated.

808
00:43:03,849 --> 00:43:07,210
[A sudden roleplay begins]
If you look at the tissue on the surface,

809
00:43:07,210 --> 00:43:10,499
[#Dr. Dong Yeon's pancake patient checkup]
You shouldn't damage the original shape.

810
00:43:11,133 --> 00:43:14,198
I suspect it might be a malignant tumor.

811
00:43:14,198 --> 00:43:17,735
Using the brown part as a guide,

812
00:43:17,735 --> 00:43:23,740
if you perform an "ectomolacpixy" carefully,
the surgery shouldn't be too difficult.

813
00:43:23,740 --> 00:43:26,810
Doctor, what is an "ectomotalase"?

814
00:43:26,810 --> 00:43:29,313
It's my medical knowledge.

815
00:43:29,313 --> 00:43:31,100
Why are you using such difficult terms?

816
00:43:31,100 --> 00:43:34,479
- You should explain it simply for the patient.
- It's not like that.

817
00:43:34,479 --> 00:43:35,771
Nurse Chae!

818
00:43:36,610 --> 00:43:37,913
Nurse Chae!

819
00:43:40,009 --> 00:43:42,637
[The kitchen turns into a clinic]
I'm sorry.

820
00:43:42,637 --> 00:43:44,802
Then what should I do?

821
00:43:45,433 --> 00:43:46,677
Who are you right now?

822
00:43:46,677 --> 00:43:48,177
- The patient.
- The patient.

823
00:43:48,884 --> 00:43:51,300
[Great actors wasting their talents]
Are you the assistant?

824
00:43:51,300 --> 00:43:53,350
[Meanwhile, You Jung coats the pasta with oil]

825
00:43:53,350 --> 00:43:56,037
So it's a pre-mixed pasta.

826
00:43:56,037 --> 00:43:58,388
[Adding tomato sauce]
In it goes!

827
00:44:02,336 --> 00:44:06,985
[Stir-fry in a pan and it's done]

828
00:44:06,985 --> 00:44:10,622
[Spread strawberry jam
and syrup on the pancakes]

829
00:44:10,622 --> 00:44:13,730
[Add fruit to finish the pancakes]
- This looks amazing. - Like it's for sale?

830
00:44:13,730 --> 00:44:15,338
Wow, it's pretty.

831
00:44:16,944 --> 00:44:20,049
[Mix apple cider vinegar with soda water]
You can just mix it with soda water.

832
00:44:22,276 --> 00:44:23,793
Wait, this is delicious.

833
00:44:23,793 --> 00:44:27,084
[Drinks are ready to go with the meal]
- It's clean and feels healthy. - Exactly.

834
00:44:27,084 --> 00:44:29,459
[Today's breakfast is complete]

835
00:44:30,416 --> 00:44:34,171
[Appetizing tomato pasta and...]

836
00:44:34,171 --> 00:44:37,513
[pancakes stacked by the members]

837
00:44:38,300 --> 00:44:40,174
- Shall we eat?
- Shall we?

838
00:44:40,174 --> 00:44:41,537
Let's eat.

839
00:44:42,185 --> 00:44:44,921
[Taking a big scoop of tomato pasta]
I really like this.

840
00:44:46,413 --> 00:44:48,237
[You Jung takes a bite too]
Like this.

841
00:44:52,259 --> 00:44:54,157
[The brow of truth]

842
00:44:54,157 --> 00:44:55,974
The tomato flavor is so good.

843
00:44:55,974 --> 00:44:57,346
Yeah, really.

844
00:44:58,418 --> 00:45:00,456
[A bite of pancake]

845
00:45:00,456 --> 00:45:03,374
I think it's really good with the fruit.

846
00:45:03,374 --> 00:45:06,482
The butter and maple scent
makes it so sweet and tasty.

847
00:45:06,482 --> 00:45:12,609
It's nice to have something low in sugar
for a light breakfast.

848
00:45:12,609 --> 00:45:13,702
Yeah.

849
00:45:14,684 --> 00:45:16,501
Why are these eggs so good?

850
00:45:16,501 --> 00:45:18,258
The eggs? Want more?

851
00:45:18,258 --> 00:45:19,471
I'll make them.

852
00:45:19,471 --> 00:45:21,325
[Orders flooding in]
- Me too. - Me too, then.

853
00:45:21,325 --> 00:45:24,313
[Naturally taking orders for everyone]
- I'll just have scrambled. - Okay.

854
00:45:25,967 --> 00:45:27,967
[Cooking scrambled eggs for five alone]

855
00:45:27,967 --> 00:45:30,459
[Checking the coast]

856
00:45:31,206 --> 00:45:34,206
[Suspicious looks are exchanged at the table]

857
00:45:35,499 --> 00:45:39,140
[Bo Gum and You Jung disappear somewhere]

858
00:45:39,140 --> 00:45:42,405
[And the man who only knows eggs]

859
00:45:42,405 --> 00:45:45,954
That was so funny.
Now that I know, it's hilarious.

860
00:45:45,954 --> 00:45:48,265
- Everyone was so funny.
- I know.

861
00:45:48,265 --> 00:45:51,153
[A cake and a mysterious box?]
- Everyone just... - Right.

862
00:45:51,967 --> 00:45:56,212
[20 days before Dong Yeon's enlistment]

863
00:45:57,039 --> 00:46:00,196
[The members prepared a surprise party]

864
00:46:00,196 --> 00:46:02,967
[The scrambled eggs are finished]

865
00:46:02,967 --> 00:46:04,674
He's coming, he's coming.

866
00:46:08,372 --> 00:46:11,548
<i>♪ Congratulations, Dong Yeon ♪</i>

867
00:46:11,548 --> 00:46:14,838
<i>♪ Congratulations, Dong Yeon ♪</i>

868
00:46:14,838 --> 00:46:17,835
[Trying to process the situation]
<i>♪ Congratulations, Dong Yeon ♪</i>

869
00:46:17,835 --> 00:46:21,391
<i>♪ Dear Dong Yeon ♪</i>

870
00:46:21,391 --> 00:46:24,508
<i>♪ Congratulations on your life ♪</i>

871
00:46:24,508 --> 00:46:27,096
[Speechless from the shock]

872
00:46:27,096 --> 00:46:30,748
- We wanted to celebrate your life.
- Oh, my gosh.

873
00:46:30,748 --> 00:46:32,342
Thank you.

874
00:46:32,342 --> 00:46:35,100
[#Who throws an enlistment party
while stir-frying eggs?]

875
00:46:35,100 --> 00:46:36,912
You Jung wrote an acrostic poem.

876
00:46:40,330 --> 00:46:43,547
Embrace a new beginning like the dawn,

877
00:46:43,547 --> 00:46:47,223
and return as strong as a lotus flower.

878
00:46:48,277 --> 00:46:50,846
You Jung, you're such a good writer.

879
00:46:50,846 --> 00:46:53,733
[Opening the gift box]
- Can I open this? - Yes, of course.

880
00:46:53,733 --> 00:46:57,783
[Enlistment gift set for Dong Yeon]
This is a gift for you.

881
00:46:57,783 --> 00:46:58,962
What's this?

882
00:47:00,703 --> 00:47:02,486
Sun stick and sunscreen.

883
00:47:02,486 --> 00:47:06,109
- The guards and insoles I've heard about.
- Guards and insoles.

884
00:47:06,109 --> 00:47:07,618
What's this?

885
00:47:07,618 --> 00:47:09,786
[Deeply moved]
This is what you need most in the army.

886
00:47:09,786 --> 00:47:11,214
That's right, that's right.

887
00:47:11,214 --> 00:47:13,640
I thought personal cutlery
would be the most useful.

888
00:47:15,533 --> 00:47:18,454
[Even a tumbler with his initials]
- This is a tumbler. - A tumbler.

889
00:47:19,277 --> 00:47:20,778
What's this?

890
00:47:20,778 --> 00:47:24,320
[The gift the members put the most effort into]

891
00:47:24,320 --> 00:47:26,083
[An album for Dong Yeon]
Who made this?

892
00:47:26,083 --> 00:47:27,437
All of us together.

893
00:47:27,437 --> 00:47:28,697
Really?

894
00:47:29,312 --> 00:47:31,261
Don't cry!

895
00:47:31,261 --> 00:47:33,436
Don't cry!

896
00:47:33,436 --> 00:47:36,232
Cry! Cry!

897
00:47:38,977 --> 00:47:40,549
This is truly amazing.

898
00:47:43,839 --> 00:47:48,967
[Photos from the past 10 years
personally chosen by the members]

899
00:47:51,113 --> 00:47:57,586
[Dong Yeon flips through each page carefully]

900
00:47:58,247 --> 00:48:01,054
Things we celebrated while traveling.

901
00:48:01,054 --> 00:48:03,427
We collected photos
from ten years ago until now.

902
00:48:03,427 --> 00:48:07,216
The photos are really in chronological order.

903
00:48:17,520 --> 00:48:19,642
[Up to recent memories]
It's all a memory.

904
00:48:22,773 --> 00:48:24,380
What's this?

905
00:48:24,380 --> 00:48:28,552
[A letter of support for Dong Yeon
on the last page]

906
00:48:28,552 --> 00:48:30,393
I'll read this later.

907
00:48:31,087 --> 00:48:35,245
[Tears imminent]
This is dangerous. This is dangerous.

908
00:48:35,245 --> 00:48:36,773
[Taking out the next gift]
What's this?

909
00:48:36,773 --> 00:48:40,156
[Coupon Set for Soldier Dong Yeon]
- They're coupons. - A "Love You" coupon?

910
00:48:40,156 --> 00:48:41,191
Let's see.

911
00:48:41,191 --> 00:48:42,206
"Bragging" coupon.

912
00:48:42,206 --> 00:48:44,454
Show off actor Kwak Dong Yeon
on personal social media.

913
00:48:46,319 --> 00:48:49,158
"Celebrity Autograph Request" coupon.

914
00:48:51,439 --> 00:48:54,352
"Listening to Military Stories" coupon.

915
00:48:54,352 --> 00:48:56,039
"Morale-Boosting Song" coupon.

916
00:48:56,039 --> 00:48:58,754
If I use this, will the Moonlight Prince
actually come visit?

917
00:49:00,099 --> 00:49:01,643
I'll go anytime.

918
00:49:02,317 --> 00:49:04,527
Thank you so much, everyone.

919
00:49:04,527 --> 00:49:06,044
I was really surprised.

920
00:49:06,044 --> 00:49:09,481
I wondered why everyone suddenly got up
after telling me to stir-fry eggs.

921
00:49:09,481 --> 00:49:11,547
Originally, we were going
to make him do the dishes.

922
00:49:11,547 --> 00:49:15,599
We planned to make him lose
so he'd have to do the dishes alone.

923
00:49:15,599 --> 00:49:17,922
[2 hours ago]

924
00:49:17,922 --> 00:49:19,683
We'll make Dong Yeon do the dishes,

925
00:49:19,683 --> 00:49:23,768
and then we can hide
and throw a surprise party.

926
00:49:23,768 --> 00:49:26,836
[Bo Gum and You Jung conspire]

927
00:49:26,836 --> 00:49:31,307
Then should we all throw
the same thing in rock-paper-scissors?

928
00:49:31,913 --> 00:49:35,344
But what if Dong Yeon wins?

929
00:49:36,339 --> 00:49:40,196
[The conspiracy ends without a solution]

930
00:49:40,196 --> 00:49:43,466
Dong Yeon almost rested
while the four of us did the dishes.

931
00:49:43,466 --> 00:49:45,688
Then we should've told him to take a short nap.

932
00:49:46,462 --> 00:49:48,832
- Serve well.
- I'll be back.

933
00:49:48,832 --> 00:49:50,360
Stay healthy.

934
00:49:53,567 --> 00:49:56,519
[After breakfast]

935
00:49:57,416 --> 00:50:00,558
[Dong Yeon takes his gifts]

936
00:50:00,558 --> 00:50:03,461
[and heads to his room]

937
00:50:06,445 --> 00:50:12,337
[He takes out the photo album again]

938
00:50:12,337 --> 00:50:17,072
[and carefully reads the letters]

939
00:50:23,996 --> 00:50:27,032
[Dong Yeon, the vitamin of Gurmi...]

940
00:50:27,032 --> 00:50:29,801
[Dong Yeon, our compass and mirror]

941
00:50:29,801 --> 00:50:33,438
[Stay healthy and safe until we meet again]

942
00:50:35,207 --> 00:50:41,030
[Letters filled with his friends' sincerity]

943
00:50:43,352 --> 00:50:48,387
[He looks through the photos one by one]

944
00:50:52,041 --> 00:50:56,862
[His friends' precious feelings
are delivered to Dong Yeon]

945
00:51:01,036 --> 00:51:03,987
- You look the same.
- You too.

946
00:51:03,987 --> 00:51:06,830
I gained weight.

947
00:51:06,830 --> 00:51:08,625
It's Byeong Yeon.

948
00:51:08,625 --> 00:51:10,099
[The Gurmi transforms one by one?]

949
00:51:11,541 --> 00:51:14,425
- You look so cool.
- We were babies back then.

950
00:51:14,425 --> 00:51:16,038
- Wow!
- This is crazy!

951
00:51:16,839 --> 00:51:18,421
- Such memories.
- Guys!

952
00:51:18,421 --> 00:51:19,516
Noona!

953
00:51:19,516 --> 00:51:21,872
- Hello.
- Hello.

954
00:51:21,872 --> 00:51:23,994
[Costume Director, Makeup Director]
- Noona! - Hello.

955
00:51:23,994 --> 00:51:25,548
- Hello.
- Hello.

956
00:51:25,548 --> 00:51:28,039
- They're here.
- How did you get here?

957
00:51:28,039 --> 00:51:31,294
[The staff who traveled a long way]
- How did you all get here? - How've you been?

958
00:51:31,294 --> 00:51:33,903
- I skipped my shoot to come.
- Wow, amazing!

959
00:51:33,903 --> 00:51:36,834
- How have you been?
- You've gotten prettier.

960
00:51:36,834 --> 00:51:38,035
Incredible!

961
00:51:38,035 --> 00:51:40,847
I was surprised you kept all the costumes.

962
00:51:40,847 --> 00:51:43,480
- I kept them, of course.
- Really?

963
00:51:43,480 --> 00:51:44,963
You guys look the same.

964
00:51:44,963 --> 00:51:46,776
- You look the same too.
- You too, Director.

965
00:51:46,776 --> 00:51:50,722
[After greeting the staff]
- Really? - Thank you.

966
00:51:50,722 --> 00:51:54,210
[In the unusually hot summer of 2016]

967
00:51:54,210 --> 00:51:57,607
[The story that made our hearts flutter]

968
00:51:57,607 --> 00:52:04,042
[Time to meet those characters again]

969
00:52:04,042 --> 00:52:06,402
[Starting now]

970
00:52:15,072 --> 00:52:16,565
<i>Who are you?</i>

971
00:52:17,539 --> 00:52:19,227
<i>Who am I?</i>

972
00:52:21,319 --> 00:52:22,598
<i>You are...</i>

973
00:52:23,772 --> 00:52:25,774
<i>the one who filled my world.</i>

974
00:52:26,411 --> 00:52:28,191
[2016 Lee Yeong]

975
00:52:28,191 --> 00:52:30,362
<i>Ra On.</i>

976
00:52:30,362 --> 00:52:36,158
[2026 Lee Yeong]

977
00:52:45,670 --> 00:52:50,580
[2016 Byeong Yeon]
<i>Lower your sword. He is the Crown Prince.</i>

978
00:52:50,580 --> 00:52:55,225
[2026 Byeong Yeon]

979
00:52:57,706 --> 00:53:01,351
<i>I am Jo Ha Yeon, daughter of Jo Man Hyeong,
the Minister of Rites.</i>

980
00:53:01,351 --> 00:53:02,445
[2016 Ha Yeon]

981
00:53:02,445 --> 00:53:07,229
[2026 Ha Yeon]
I really wanted to meet you again.

982
00:53:13,541 --> 00:53:17,600
[2016 Yoon Seong]
<i>You really fell.</i>

983
00:53:17,600 --> 00:53:21,471
[2026 Yoon Seong]
A star.

984
00:53:39,201 --> 00:53:42,667
[2016 Ra On]

985
00:53:42,667 --> 00:53:48,504
[2026 Ra On]

986
00:53:57,087 --> 00:53:59,036
[Facing each other in costumes
from 10 years ago]

987
00:53:59,036 --> 00:54:00,937
Welcome.

988
00:54:00,937 --> 00:54:03,046
I am Hong Ra On, Your Highness.

989
00:54:03,046 --> 00:54:06,429
You are Ra On, who filled my world.

990
00:54:06,429 --> 00:54:07,717
You, Sam Nom!

991
00:54:07,717 --> 00:54:10,593
[Laughter erupts at the 10-year reunion]
Why is this so funny?

992
00:54:10,593 --> 00:54:12,282
Go up there and sit down.

993
00:54:12,282 --> 00:54:14,265
Wow, how does everyone feel?

994
00:54:14,265 --> 00:54:16,795
We were talking about it
while waiting for everyone to arrive.

995
00:54:16,795 --> 00:54:20,830
How did we film in this heat in these clothes?

996
00:54:20,830 --> 00:54:25,628
They must have matched the weather to back then
to celebrate the 10th anniversary.

997
00:54:25,628 --> 00:54:29,124
- It's like they're blasting heaters at us.
- Exactly.

998
00:54:29,886 --> 00:54:31,863
By the way, did the clothes fit everyone?

999
00:54:31,863 --> 00:54:33,796
They're exactly the same.

1000
00:54:33,796 --> 00:54:37,767
It feels like you're filming
episode 19 of Love in the Moonlight.

1001
00:54:37,767 --> 00:54:40,850
[Freeze-dried for 10 years]
Episode 19? Not 190?

1002
00:54:40,850 --> 00:54:43,145
For me, the belt feels a bit...

1003
00:54:43,145 --> 00:54:45,030
- A bit tight?
- Oh, really?

1004
00:54:45,030 --> 00:54:46,689
It's gotten a bit smaller.

1005
00:54:46,689 --> 00:54:50,472
[But the face is still radiant]
It makes me realize how slim I was back then.

1006
00:54:50,472 --> 00:54:52,141
I think the clothes got bigger.

1007
00:54:52,141 --> 00:54:54,077
You Jung lost weight.

1008
00:54:54,077 --> 00:54:58,335
But really, when I saw You Jung
come out in her makeup earlier...

1009
00:54:58,335 --> 00:55:00,238
- She felt very mature.
- She has matured.

1010
00:55:00,238 --> 00:55:02,337
[From a girl to a lady]
She's become more of a woman.

1011
00:55:02,337 --> 00:55:04,074
[Stretching his neck]
She's matured.

1012
00:55:04,074 --> 00:55:06,049
- She's more of a woman now.
- Definitely.

1013
00:55:06,049 --> 00:55:08,137
I can't see because of Dong Yeon.

1014
00:55:08,137 --> 00:55:10,285
[The gat is blocking the view]
I can't see because of Dong Yeon.

1015
00:55:10,285 --> 00:55:12,702
- Me too.
- Every time Dong Yeon turns his head...

1016
00:55:12,702 --> 00:55:15,812
- This is sharp. I feel like it'll stab me.
- Sorry, sorry.

1017
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:18,427
No, it's okay. It can't be helped.
It's your signature look.

1018
00:55:18,427 --> 00:55:21,284
But how does it feel to wear a wig
after such a long time?

1019
00:55:21,284 --> 00:55:25,267
[Byeong Yeon's meticulously crafted wig]

1020
00:55:25,267 --> 00:55:27,480
[Once it's placed on Dong Yeon's head...]

1021
00:55:27,480 --> 00:55:31,300
[Warrior Byeong Yeon is complete]
I'm used to it now.

1022
00:55:31,300 --> 00:55:33,563
The feeling of these bangs on my lips...

1023
00:55:33,563 --> 00:55:36,820
And the feeling of these stray hairs
sticking to my sweat.

1024
00:55:36,820 --> 00:55:38,201
It's been so long.

1025
00:55:38,201 --> 00:55:40,108
But it's a bit thinner than back then.

1026
00:55:41,356 --> 00:55:43,073
It's a bit lighter. A layered cut.

1027
00:55:43,073 --> 00:55:47,964
But once he's in character as Kim hyung,
he suddenly looks sharp.

1028
00:55:47,964 --> 00:55:50,132
Right. He looks a bit chic.

1029
00:55:50,132 --> 00:55:52,055
- Cynical.
- His eyes are a bit...

1030
00:55:52,055 --> 00:55:54,222
A bit scary to talk to.

1031
00:55:54,222 --> 00:55:56,867
Did you see what I sent?
When we were preparing for this.

1032
00:55:56,867 --> 00:55:58,008
Yes, the blog post.

1033
00:55:58,008 --> 00:56:02,199
A blogger organized all the famous lines

1034
00:56:02,199 --> 00:56:05,575
- from episodes 1 to 18.
- Really?

1035
00:56:05,575 --> 00:56:08,131
There were so many good lines.

1036
00:56:08,131 --> 00:56:09,973
This one is my favorite.

1037
00:56:09,973 --> 00:56:13,924
"Who knows if the memory of being loved
will be the strength to live a lifetime?"

1038
00:56:13,924 --> 00:56:15,010
Me too.

1039
00:56:15,010 --> 00:56:20,103
[#Ra On's sincerity to Lee Yeong]
<i>I don't reach out thinking I'll touch the sky.</i>

1040
00:56:23,808 --> 00:56:28,003
<i>Can I not confess to someone
I can never be with?</i>

1041
00:56:28,884 --> 00:56:33,422
<i>Letting go with a warm heart
is as meaningful as love.</i>

1042
00:56:34,655 --> 00:56:41,584
<i>Who knows if the memory of being loved
will be the strength to live a lifetime?</i>

1043
00:56:45,467 --> 00:56:49,070
[After a moment of nostalgia]
- She's like Dr. Oh Eun Young. - Exactly.

1044
00:56:49,855 --> 00:56:51,655
It's so good.

1045
00:56:56,230 --> 00:56:59,295
- I'm getting goosebumps.
- You look like Ra On now, right?

1046
00:56:59,295 --> 00:57:03,467
[You Jung transforms once again?]
It feels a bit strange to be like this.

1047
00:57:03,467 --> 00:57:05,996
[From lady Hong Ra On to eunuch Hong Sam Nom]

1048
00:57:05,996 --> 00:57:09,099
The person with the richest heart
in all of Joseon...

1049
00:57:09,099 --> 00:57:12,870
This is a gift from me, Hong Sam Nom.

1050
00:57:14,643 --> 00:57:17,132
[Bo Gum from a scholar to the Crown Prince]

1051
00:57:17,132 --> 00:57:20,523
But I'm going to try it.

1052
00:57:21,849 --> 00:57:23,365
That forbidden love.

1053
00:57:25,200 --> 00:57:28,351
[The Gurmi with the Prince and Ra On]
- Watch it! - Watch it!

1054
00:57:28,351 --> 00:57:30,639
Kim hyung, where are we going?

1055
00:57:31,406 --> 00:57:33,849
[Heading somewhere as they did 10 years ago]
Just follow me.

1056
00:57:37,326 --> 00:57:40,069
[The car they'll be traveling in arrives]

1057
00:57:40,069 --> 00:57:42,306
- The car is nice.
- It's so good.

1058
00:57:42,306 --> 00:57:45,362
[Spacious enough for five people]
- It's huge. - It's really big.

1059
00:57:45,362 --> 00:57:46,982
Are we heading out?

1060
00:57:50,126 --> 00:57:52,088
But the car is really spacious.

1061
00:57:52,088 --> 00:57:54,764
- It really is.
- My Ikseongwan is tall, but it doesn't touch.

1062
00:57:54,764 --> 00:57:56,273
- You're right.
- It doesn't touch.

1063
00:57:56,273 --> 00:57:57,274
I see.

1064
00:57:57,274 --> 00:58:00,176
Wait, is there a massage function in front?

1065
00:58:00,176 --> 00:58:03,079
[Massage function ON]
Oh, should I try it? This is pretty nice.

1066
00:58:03,079 --> 00:58:04,616
It's really good.

1067
00:58:04,616 --> 00:58:08,069
[Enjoying a refreshing drive]
- This is refreshing. - It's quite cool.

1068
00:58:09,985 --> 00:58:12,129
But I was really grateful.

1069
00:58:12,129 --> 00:58:15,111
- Jin A and Soon Jeong...
- That's right.

1070
00:58:15,111 --> 00:58:17,394
- Jin Hee and everyone for coming.
- For coming.

1071
00:58:17,394 --> 00:58:20,183
- It felt a bit strange, didn't it?
- It did.

1072
00:58:20,183 --> 00:58:23,318
It felt like wearing my old school uniform
after graduating.

1073
00:58:24,553 --> 00:58:27,744
When I put on the solo dance costume,

1074
00:58:27,744 --> 00:58:32,375
it was just pretty and nice
to see it after so long,

1075
00:58:32,375 --> 00:58:35,810
but wearing the eunuch uniform
feels really strange.

1076
00:58:35,810 --> 00:58:37,473
- It feels like you've gone back?
- Yeah.

1077
00:58:37,473 --> 00:58:40,437
You Jung looked like
she was on the verge of tears

1078
00:58:40,437 --> 00:58:43,125
when we met after getting ready.

1079
00:58:43,125 --> 00:58:44,854
[Facing friends as Hong Sam Nom]

1080
00:58:44,854 --> 00:58:46,451
That's usually Bo Gum's role.

1081
00:58:46,451 --> 00:58:48,016
- Exactly.
- Bo Gum's body has matured.

1082
00:58:48,016 --> 00:58:51,207
- What?
- No, it hasn't.

1083
00:58:51,207 --> 00:58:53,784
Is it because he's a man in his mid-30s now?

1084
00:58:53,784 --> 00:58:56,331
- Don't attack me with his age.
- He's become a grown man.

1085
00:58:57,462 --> 00:59:00,784
But Bo Gum, this project

1086
00:59:00,784 --> 00:59:03,513
was like a bucket list item for you.

1087
00:59:03,513 --> 00:59:05,428
- That's right.
- How do you feel?

1088
00:59:05,428 --> 00:59:08,698
I'm so proud and grateful.

1089
00:59:08,698 --> 00:59:10,252
Is there anything else you want to do?

1090
00:59:10,252 --> 00:59:14,255
It'd be nice to meet again in ten years.

1091
00:59:14,255 --> 00:59:18,561
Then will we only meet in ten years
after we part ways today?

1092
00:59:18,561 --> 00:59:21,998
No. We should meet every time
Dong Yeon is on leave.

1093
00:59:21,998 --> 00:59:23,333
We talked about that.

1094
00:59:23,333 --> 00:59:26,065
- Let's all go in one car.
- That'll be fun.

1095
00:59:26,065 --> 00:59:29,877
- We'll visit him as if we're on a trip.
- That'll be fun.

1096
00:59:29,877 --> 00:59:34,353
[Laughing and chatting,
they soon reach their destination]

1097
00:59:34,353 --> 00:59:38,593
[A place full of fresh greenery]

1098
00:59:38,593 --> 00:59:42,224
[Where flowers bloom and the wind lingers]

1099
00:59:43,867 --> 00:59:47,127
[Mysterious lighting equipment is set up]

1100
00:59:47,127 --> 00:59:50,939
[Is someone waiting for the Gurmi?]

1101
00:59:53,608 --> 00:59:57,953
[The Gurmi finally arrives]
- It's beautiful. - What a pretty place.

1102
00:59:57,953 --> 01:00:00,767
- Hello.
- How are you?

1103
01:00:00,767 --> 01:00:03,746
[Someone greets them with a familiar face]
Hello.

1104
01:00:03,746 --> 01:00:07,579
[Wearing the same hanbok as 10 years ago]

1105
01:00:07,579 --> 01:00:12,714
[The one who captured their images back then]

1106
01:00:12,714 --> 01:00:15,785
[They meet the photographer
from that day again]

1107
01:00:15,785 --> 01:00:18,346
- We're meeting again after ten years.
- We really are.

1108
01:00:18,346 --> 01:00:19,743
Thank you for coming all this way.

1109
01:00:19,743 --> 01:00:24,781
We took a group photo when we shot
the drama posters, right?

1110
01:00:24,781 --> 01:00:26,389
Yes, we did.

1111
01:00:26,389 --> 01:00:29,362
- It was never released.
- It never went public.

1112
01:00:29,362 --> 01:00:33,241
We can just replace it
with what we shoot today.

1113
01:00:33,241 --> 01:00:37,123
[Taking a poster for the 10th anniversary]
Let's start. Yes, good.

1114
01:00:37,123 --> 01:00:39,192
Give me a happy expression. Yes.

1115
01:00:40,248 --> 01:00:42,310
[Somewhat awkward]

1116
01:00:42,310 --> 01:00:45,722
Now, just a soft smile. Yes.

1117
01:00:45,722 --> 01:00:47,189
A soft smile.

1118
01:00:49,613 --> 01:00:53,535
[Awkward to strike a pose in front of friends]

1119
01:00:55,054 --> 01:00:57,724
- This is quite...
- This kind of vibe.

1120
01:00:57,724 --> 01:01:00,323
Beautiful. Good.

1121
01:01:00,323 --> 01:01:06,102
[Reliving the memories,
capturing themselves ten years later]

1122
01:01:06,102 --> 01:01:12,145
Taking photos in hanbok like this,
everything felt just the same.

1123
01:01:12,145 --> 01:01:14,777
It's so similar. It's just like back then.

1124
01:01:14,777 --> 01:01:16,059
It's beautiful.

1125
01:01:16,059 --> 01:01:18,967
We've never really gone on
a proper trip together before.

1126
01:01:18,967 --> 01:01:23,071
[The Gurmi's First Friendship Trip]
Except for that one backpacking trip.

1127
01:01:24,125 --> 01:01:28,296
It was so much fun, and time just flew by.

1128
01:01:28,296 --> 01:01:31,761
The time we spent rafting
with all five of us was fun, too.

1129
01:01:33,090 --> 01:01:37,986
For our 20th anniversary, maybe we'll
do something even better than water sports.

1130
01:01:38,848 --> 01:01:40,674
Rock-paper-scissors!

1131
01:01:40,674 --> 01:01:44,145
Just chatting about small things
was the most enjoyable part.

1132
01:01:44,145 --> 01:01:47,318
Why do the five of us
become so childish when we're together?

1133
01:01:48,163 --> 01:01:52,648
We even got to see
the Moonlight Princes' debut.

1134
01:01:52,648 --> 01:01:55,745
When we sang "Misty Road,"
I felt really touched because...

1135
01:01:55,745 --> 01:01:58,993
it was so clear that we were all being sincere.

1136
01:01:59,774 --> 01:02:02,852
- What will the next ten years be like?
- Thank you.

1137
01:02:02,852 --> 01:02:06,083
Starting families,
having housewarming parties...

1138
01:02:06,083 --> 01:02:08,715
I hope we become like
next-door neighbors or cousins.

1139
01:02:10,023 --> 01:02:14,418
"Who knows if the memory of being loved
will be the strength to live a lifetime?"

1140
01:02:14,418 --> 01:02:16,070
There was a line like that in the drama.

1141
01:02:16,070 --> 01:02:18,627
So, to me, "Love in the Moonlight" is...

1142
01:02:19,301 --> 01:02:21,437
the strength to live my whole life.

1143
01:02:21,437 --> 01:02:23,339
A bundle of gifts.

1144
01:02:23,339 --> 01:02:25,370
A living memory.

1145
01:02:25,370 --> 01:02:27,702
A midsummer getaway.

1146
01:02:27,702 --> 01:02:29,510
It's "Ra On."

1147
01:02:29,510 --> 01:02:33,055
The fact that we can still be full of joy
even after ten years...

1148
01:02:33,055 --> 01:02:35,558
and that we can still laugh together...

1149
01:02:35,558 --> 01:02:38,902
I think that's true joy and happiness.

1150
01:02:38,902 --> 01:02:42,870
The fact that you still remember
and cherish those memories with us...

1151
01:02:42,870 --> 01:02:46,860
is a really great source of motivation.

1152
01:02:46,860 --> 01:02:50,336
I think that power allows us
to keep moving forward.

1153
01:02:50,336 --> 01:02:54,637
We'll stay close so we can see you again
in 20 or 30 years.

1154
01:02:54,637 --> 01:02:57,647
Please keep cheering us on. Thank you.

1155
01:02:57,647 --> 01:03:01,215
Always be healthy and happy. Thank you.

1156
01:03:02,348 --> 01:03:04,390
- The last slate.
- Yes.

1157
01:03:04,390 --> 01:03:09,296
Calling it the last slate makes it feel like
we're wrapping up these ten years.

1158
01:03:09,897 --> 01:03:11,866
One, two, three.

1159
01:03:12,741 --> 01:03:17,266
I sincerely hope that everyone's lives
will always be full of "Ra On."

1160
01:03:17,266 --> 01:03:18,912
Thank you.
